WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:00:49.353 --> 00:00:52.231
- Hi. How are you?
- I'm good. Thanks.


00:00:52.314 --> 00:00:53.667
Who do I make this out to?


00:00:53.691 --> 00:00:55.067
Uh, Bobbi with an "I".


00:00:59.405 --> 00:01:01.740
In the prologue,
you say you wrote this book


00:01:01.824 --> 00:01:03.664
in order to better understand
and accept death.


00:01:04.326 --> 00:01:05.536
Um...


00:01:05.619 --> 00:01:07.788
Yeah. It feels unnatural to me.


00:01:07.871 --> 00:01:10.124
I can't accept that something
alive has to die.


00:01:10.207 --> 00:01:11.250
Thank you.


00:01:12.668 --> 00:01:13.669
- Ingrid...
- Mm.


00:01:13.752 --> 00:01:15.170
We've fulfilled the hour.


00:01:15.254 --> 00:01:16.565
I mean, in fact, we've gone over.


00:01:16.589 --> 00:01:18.349
Well, there's still a
lot of people waiting.


00:01:18.882 --> 00:01:20.759
Yes. We'll do what you want.


00:01:20.843 --> 00:01:21.969
Could you sign mine?


00:01:22.052 --> 00:01:24.346
Stella! I didn't see you.


00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.056
Why didn't you come straight up?


00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:27.558
I was embarrassed.


00:01:27.641 --> 00:01:28.809
You draw a crowd!


00:01:28.892 --> 00:01:30.328
- A lot of young people.
- Thank you.


00:01:30.352 --> 00:01:31.687
Not just women.


00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.856
Stella, this is Anne.
Anne, my friend Stella.


00:01:33.939 --> 00:01:35.250
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.


00:01:35.274 --> 00:01:37.002
I'm gonna stay until
I've signed for everybody.


00:01:37.026 --> 00:01:39.528
Yes. I'll just make sure that
no one else joins the line.


00:01:39.612 --> 00:01:40.654
Okay.


00:01:41.488 --> 00:01:43.490
Oh, I haven't seen you in forever.


00:01:43.574 --> 00:01:44.992
I'm living in Boston now.


00:01:45.075 --> 00:01:46.535
I came to see my son,


00:01:46.619 --> 00:01:48.203
and to visit Martha in the hospital.


00:01:50.122 --> 00:01:51.957
You know she has cancer, right?


00:01:52.041 --> 00:01:53.042
It's a bad one.


00:01:53.125 --> 00:01:54.335
Martha?


00:01:54.418 --> 00:01:55.418
Martha Hunt?


00:01:55.461 --> 00:01:56.462
Yes.


00:01:56.545 --> 00:01:58.422
She's at Manhattan Memorial
Cancer Center.


00:01:58.505 --> 00:01:59.665
I thought you would've heard.


00:02:00.257 --> 00:02:02.057
No. To be honest,
I haven't seen her in years.


00:02:02.092 --> 00:02:04.303
Martha is sick? I can't imagine it.


00:02:04.386 --> 00:02:06.764
If you go see her,
it'll make her very happy.


00:02:06.847 --> 00:02:08.432
Yeah. Of course.


00:02:08.515 --> 00:02:09.767
Of course I will.


00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:13.479
Um, thank you so much for coming.
I really appreciate it.


00:02:13.562 --> 00:02:14.605
Congratulations.


00:02:14.688 --> 00:02:15.689
- Thank you.
- Mm!


00:02:15.773 --> 00:02:16.916
- I'll see you soon.
- Thanks.


00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:17.941
- Bye.
- Bye.


00:02:20.819 --> 00:02:21.820
Hi.


00:02:23.947 --> 00:02:26.158
- Who do I make this out to?
- Frances.


00:02:27.493 --> 00:02:30.079
- Is that you?
- No, it's my girlfriend.


00:02:30.162 --> 00:02:31.163
She really admires you.


00:02:31.955 --> 00:02:33.540
- So do I.
- Thank you.


00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.880
Could you write "It won't happen again"?


00:02:42.383 --> 00:02:43.550
Of course I can.


00:02:44.677 --> 00:02:47.054
Yes. Thank you. It won't happen again.


00:02:49.431 --> 00:02:50.431
I hope not.


00:03:06.615 --> 00:03:09.159
Hi. I'm here to see Martha Hunt.


00:03:09.243 --> 00:03:10.869
I think she's on the 16th floor.


00:03:10.953 --> 00:03:12.204
Okay. One sec.


00:03:14.748 --> 00:03:17.084
Yes. Room 1614.


00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:19.336
The elevator is at the end
of the hall, on the left.


00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:20.587
- Thanks.
- No problem.


00:03:42.651 --> 00:03:43.652
Martha?


00:03:45.154 --> 00:03:46.238
Ingrid!


00:03:47.406 --> 00:03:49.908
What a surprise!


00:03:49.992 --> 00:03:52.161
- How did you hear?
- I ran into Stella.


00:03:52.244 --> 00:03:53.746
- She told me.
- Oh.


00:03:54.913 --> 00:03:57.875
I'm so sorry, I didn't
even know you were sick.


00:03:57.958 --> 00:04:00.586
Oh, well, you with your work
and me with mine.


00:04:00.669 --> 00:04:03.297
I mean, time's gotten away from us.


00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.007
Yes, and I was living in Paris.


00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:07.885
Yeah, I heard.
I've been reading about you.


00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:10.012
I know you have published another book


00:04:10.095 --> 00:04:11.847
and it's doing very well.


00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.474
Thank you.


00:04:14.099 --> 00:04:15.100
So...


00:04:16.226 --> 00:04:17.227
How are you?


00:04:18.479 --> 00:04:20.606
I'm sure you're sick of telling everybody.


00:04:21.607 --> 00:04:24.485
Well, it's cervical cancer. Stage three.


00:04:25.027 --> 00:04:27.821
It isn't operable,
but they're treating me, so


00:04:27.905 --> 00:04:30.282
looks like I'm not gonna die quite yet.


00:04:31.325 --> 00:04:36.455
Um, I've become a guinea pig
for an experimental treatment


00:04:36.538 --> 00:04:38.832
and the results are better
than the doctors expected.


00:04:38.916 --> 00:04:39.958
- Great!
- Yeah.


00:04:40.042 --> 00:04:42.377
That's great! Well, you seem
like you're in good spirits.


00:04:43.253 --> 00:04:46.465
Well, I swing between
euphoria and depression.


00:04:46.548 --> 00:04:47.883
Oh, I'm so sorry.


00:04:47.966 --> 00:04:51.261
No, it's normal,
and the doctors warned me, you know.


00:04:51.804 --> 00:04:53.138
- Highs and lows.
- Mm-hmm.


00:04:54.014 --> 00:04:55.057
Mm-hmm.


00:04:56.016 --> 00:04:57.559
It will sound absurd,


00:04:58.519 --> 00:05:01.897
but after all the accepting
and preparing to face the end,


00:05:03.357 --> 00:05:06.026
survival feels almost disappointing.


00:05:06.109 --> 00:05:07.319
Oh, don't say that.


00:05:07.402 --> 00:05:09.154
No, I was prepared to leave.


00:05:12.074 --> 00:05:15.661
In fact, when they gave me
the initial diagnosis,


00:05:16.245 --> 00:05:17.347
I didn't want any treatment.


00:05:17.371 --> 00:05:18.997
Well, I'm glad you changed your mind.


00:05:20.499 --> 00:05:23.335
'Cause, you know, just the thought...


00:05:23.418 --> 00:05:25.045
And that I wouldn't know...


00:05:25.128 --> 00:05:27.381
Anyway, I realized that I really...


00:05:28.048 --> 00:05:31.385
I'm not ready to abandon
the party just yet.


00:05:32.344 --> 00:05:35.722
But I had truly gotten used to the idea.


00:05:36.598 --> 00:05:39.226
Well, I suppose that it's good
to get used to the idea,


00:05:39.309 --> 00:05:40.686
but without giving up, right?


00:05:41.937 --> 00:05:43.657
You've been through
a lot of wars, remember?


00:05:44.356 --> 00:05:46.108
I live with them every day.


00:05:49.152 --> 00:05:52.239
Oh, Ingrid, I'm so happy to see you.


00:05:52.322 --> 00:05:54.575
I almost called you a thousand times.


00:05:54.658 --> 00:05:55.784
- I'm sorry.
- Me, too!


00:05:55.868 --> 00:05:57.748
It's ridiculous that
we haven't seen each other.


00:05:57.786 --> 00:06:00.414
I promise I'm gonna visit
until you get sick of me.


00:06:00.497 --> 00:06:01.832
Will you?


00:06:01.915 --> 00:06:03.333
You promise?


00:06:03.417 --> 00:06:04.960
I'm gonna hold you to that.


00:06:05.043 --> 00:06:06.503
Your daughter knows, I guess.


00:06:07.713 --> 00:06:08.714
Yes.


00:06:10.382 --> 00:06:14.303
When I first made up my mind
to forgo any treatment,


00:06:14.386 --> 00:06:15.470
I told her,


00:06:16.805 --> 00:06:17.931
and she just said...


00:06:19.141 --> 00:06:20.309
"It's your choice."


00:06:21.518 --> 00:06:22.895
Period.


00:06:22.978 --> 00:06:24.771
As if it was something trivial,


00:06:26.023 --> 00:06:27.858
something that had
nothing to do with her.


00:06:29.526 --> 00:06:31.069
How are you two getting along?


00:06:31.153 --> 00:06:33.196
Um, same as ever.


00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:34.698
We're barely in touch.


00:06:34.781 --> 00:06:36.158
What does she do?


00:06:36.241 --> 00:06:37.326
She's doing well.


00:06:37.409 --> 00:06:40.829
She is, uh, an agent
for classical musicians.


00:06:44.041 --> 00:06:45.459
It might sound horrible,


00:06:47.336 --> 00:06:50.047
but I don't feel like she's my daughter.


00:06:52.174 --> 00:06:55.469
I fantasize frequently about
her being swapped at birth.


00:06:55.552 --> 00:06:56.845
What?


00:06:56.929 --> 00:06:59.598
What are you talking about?
She looks just like you.


00:06:59.681 --> 00:07:00.891
She has your face.


00:07:02.559 --> 00:07:05.437
I never interested her as a mother.


00:07:06.521 --> 00:07:07.564
Why not?


00:07:07.648 --> 00:07:09.775
I was a teenager when I had her.


00:07:11.276 --> 00:07:13.278
I didn't know what to do with a baby.


00:07:14.696 --> 00:07:17.991
And when we started working at
<i>Paper Magazine,</i> you remember?


00:07:18.075 --> 00:07:19.785
We practically lived at night.


00:07:20.327 --> 00:07:22.371
You remember New York in the '80s?


00:07:22.454 --> 00:07:23.497
Yeah.


00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:25.666
Anything important happened at night.


00:07:29.378 --> 00:07:32.839
And then I went to work
as a war correspondent,


00:07:32.923 --> 00:07:34.174
traveling constantly.


00:07:34.716 --> 00:07:36.093
And that didn't help.


00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:39.596
My work just completely took over.


00:07:43.225 --> 00:07:46.728
I was never what a mother
is supposed to be.


00:07:49.022 --> 00:07:52.526
But Michelle started to hate me


00:07:52.609 --> 00:07:54.403
long before I was away so much.


00:07:56.738 --> 00:08:00.075
I remember feeling her resentment
even when she was a little girl.


00:08:03.453 --> 00:08:05.414
She made herself very clear.


00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:14.673
She couldn't bear... not having a father.


00:08:16.508 --> 00:08:21.596
She saw other girls with their fathers
and she wanted to know about hers.


00:08:24.558 --> 00:08:27.310
At first, I told her
I didn't know who he was, but...


00:08:29.855 --> 00:08:31.314
It kind of made things worse.


00:08:33.817 --> 00:08:34.860
<i>I was lying to her.</i>


00:08:36.194 --> 00:08:38.363
<i>Of course I knew
who her father was.</i>


00:08:39.281 --> 00:08:40.741
<i>His name was Fred.</i>


00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.541
<i>We dated for a few months
before he was drafted.</i>


00:08:50.542 --> 00:08:53.920
<i>And then went away to fight,
towards the end of Vietnam.</i>


00:08:55.589 --> 00:08:59.384
<i>When he came back,
a year later, he was</i>


00:08:59.468 --> 00:09:00.927
<i>somebody different.</i>


00:09:01.011 --> 00:09:03.346
Fred! What happened?


00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.223
<i>He was a broken toy.</i>


00:09:06.892 --> 00:09:09.269
Hey. Hey, it's okay.


00:09:09.352 --> 00:09:12.564
I'm here. It's all over now, Fred.
You're back home.


00:09:12.647 --> 00:09:14.024
But it's not over for me.


00:09:16.902 --> 00:09:18.945
I still got the war inside my head.


00:09:21.281 --> 00:09:22.616
I can't get free of it.


00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:26.995
I hallucinate every single day.


00:09:29.956 --> 00:09:32.542
And I was high practically all the time.


00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:39.007
I don't know what I'm doing with my life,


00:09:40.467 --> 00:09:41.968
but I'm not staying here.


00:09:46.681 --> 00:09:47.724
It's all right.


00:09:49.267 --> 00:09:50.852
Feel free to do what you like.


00:09:51.937 --> 00:09:53.855
Think about what's best for you.


00:09:58.151 --> 00:09:59.152
Okay.


00:10:01.321 --> 00:10:02.405
Thanks.


00:10:07.911 --> 00:10:08.912
Can I kiss you?


00:10:38.275 --> 00:10:40.193
- Does Michelle know this?
- Oh.


00:10:42.279 --> 00:10:45.699
She started asking about her father
as soon as she could talk.


00:10:49.536 --> 00:10:52.956
But it's not something
you can explain to a child, right?


00:10:54.624 --> 00:10:57.627
By puberty, she carved out
quite an abyss between us.


00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.130
It came to define her adolescence.


00:11:02.215 --> 00:11:03.967
But, by then, I was no longer there.


00:11:05.343 --> 00:11:08.680
I was in New York, with you,
living my life.


00:11:11.183 --> 00:11:14.936
<i>I arranged to meet Fred one evening
to tell him about the situation.</i>


00:11:15.478 --> 00:11:17.772
So, I took a first aid course


00:11:18.523 --> 00:11:21.318
and, because I'm a war veteran,
they've hired me at a hospital,


00:11:21.401 --> 00:11:22.444
down in San Diego.


00:11:24.821 --> 00:11:26.364
It's good news, right?


00:11:27.991 --> 00:11:29.659
I have some news for you too.


00:11:31.536 --> 00:11:32.537
I'm pregnant.


00:11:34.414 --> 00:11:37.250
- You're pregnant?
- Yes.


00:11:39.461 --> 00:11:41.838
But I was planning on moving
to San Diego next week.


00:11:44.216 --> 00:11:45.467
Then what are we gonna do?


00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:48.637
Whatever I do, my parents
will support me, so...


00:11:49.346 --> 00:11:50.347
I'm not alone.


00:11:52.599 --> 00:11:53.600
Mm.


00:11:55.936 --> 00:11:57.604
I don't think working in a hospital


00:11:57.687 --> 00:11:59.940
was the best thing
for such a damaged person.


00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.067
It's the closest thing to war.


00:12:03.235 --> 00:12:04.778
He needed therapy and rehab.


00:12:05.362 --> 00:12:07.530
Yeah, that would have been
more sensible,


00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:10.659
but he wanted to be useful,


00:12:12.077 --> 00:12:13.411
to ease his conscience.


00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:18.333
He believed that helping people
between life and death


00:12:18.416 --> 00:12:22.337
was his best chance
of getting back any peace.


00:12:24.047 --> 00:12:26.758
I could only free him
of any responsibility.


00:12:27.926 --> 00:12:30.053
He left before Michelle was born.


00:12:30.762 --> 00:12:31.805
He never knew her.


00:12:34.933 --> 00:12:38.395
He didn't call once to ask about her.


00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:41.523
When did you tell her?


00:12:42.148 --> 00:12:43.817
She was about 12.


00:12:45.485 --> 00:12:48.154
She wanted to know
where he was living,


00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:50.532
and I didn't know anymore.


00:12:52.075 --> 00:12:53.702
She was so insistent


00:12:54.661 --> 00:12:58.373
that I tracked down an old friend of his
from high school,


00:12:59.916 --> 00:13:04.546
who told me that Fred
had gotten married


00:13:04.629 --> 00:13:06.506
and had recently died.


00:13:08.216 --> 00:13:11.594
I asked him for his wife's number,


00:13:12.679 --> 00:13:14.097
and then I called her.


00:13:15.098 --> 00:13:16.683
I wanted to know what had happened.


00:13:18.435 --> 00:13:22.897
<i>She told me they were
coming home after a trip.</i>


00:13:25.984 --> 00:13:27.152
Is that smoke?


00:13:28.445 --> 00:13:29.446
Yes.


00:13:30.613 --> 00:13:32.198
Something's on fire.


00:13:32.907 --> 00:13:33.992
There's a house on fire.


00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:38.496
We should call the fire department.


00:13:45.503 --> 00:13:47.505
- Stop the car.
- Fred...


00:13:54.346 --> 00:13:55.847
What are you doing?


00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:57.557
- I'm gonna take a look.
- No!


00:13:57.640 --> 00:13:59.642
That's crazy! Fred!


00:13:59.726 --> 00:14:02.145
- There might be someone inside.
- Fred, stop! Stop!


00:14:02.228 --> 00:14:05.565
Don't go in. It's dangerous!
Look at me, I'm here.


00:14:05.648 --> 00:14:08.485
Let's find a gas station
and call the fire department, please.


00:14:08.568 --> 00:14:09.652
Don't you hear the screams?


00:14:10.153 --> 00:14:11.946
No, I don't hear anything.


00:14:14.074 --> 00:14:16.743
Fred, please! Fred! Fred!


00:14:17.869 --> 00:14:19.245
Fred, don't go in there!


00:14:22.248 --> 00:14:23.708
Don't you hear the screams?


00:14:23.792 --> 00:14:25.710
There's someone inside crying for help!


00:14:27.796 --> 00:14:28.838
Fred!


00:14:40.683 --> 00:14:42.894
Sir! Sir!


00:14:42.977 --> 00:14:44.938
Please, help me!


00:14:45.021 --> 00:14:47.315
- Sir! Sir, please!
- Let's go!


00:14:47.399 --> 00:14:49.609
- Please, my husband's inside!
- Ladder up!


00:14:49.692 --> 00:14:51.277
Sir! My husband's inside!


00:14:51.361 --> 00:14:52.654
My husband's inside!


00:14:52.737 --> 00:14:54.173
He thought he heard
voices crying for help.


00:14:54.197 --> 00:14:55.633
Put two lines on the back side, guys!


00:14:55.657 --> 00:14:58.576
He went into the house trying to save
whoever was trapped by the fire.


00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:00.179
Okay, get back in your car.
Do not go over there.


00:15:00.203 --> 00:15:01.204
I will stay here. Okay.


00:15:01.287 --> 00:15:02.473
Please, ma'am. Is there someone else?


00:15:02.497 --> 00:15:04.297
- No, I don't know!
- Ladder up, guys! Ladder!


00:15:04.374 --> 00:15:05.414
There's a civilian inside!


00:15:05.458 --> 00:15:06.898
Get back in your car, ma'am, please.


00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.870
All right, get in there!
Get in that top window.


00:15:12.298 --> 00:15:15.093
There you go. It's gonna blow out.


00:15:17.679 --> 00:15:18.721
Good boys.


00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:30.080
I'm sorry, there was nothing we could do.


00:15:33.069 --> 00:15:34.904
He didn't get to the second floor.


00:15:36.072 --> 00:15:38.366
He must have passed out
from the smoke and the flames.


00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:39.701
And the other bodies?


00:15:39.784 --> 00:15:40.952
There was nobody else.


00:15:41.035 --> 00:15:43.288
This house has been abandoned
for a long time.


00:15:43.371 --> 00:15:44.491
There was only your husband.


00:15:44.539 --> 00:15:45.748
But he


00:15:47.083 --> 00:15:49.294
he told me he heard screams for help...


00:15:49.377 --> 00:15:50.712
Impossible, ma'am.


00:15:52.088 --> 00:15:53.131
There was no one else.


00:15:54.174 --> 00:15:55.216
It's true.


00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.512
I didn't hear the screams either.


00:16:01.222 --> 00:16:04.142
I tried to stop him from going in, but...


00:16:05.477 --> 00:16:06.519
I didn't.


00:16:06.603 --> 00:16:07.812
He was very brave.


00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:10.482
Did you tell Michelle all of this?


00:16:10.565 --> 00:16:12.442
I had to give her every detail.


00:16:13.401 --> 00:16:16.321
I even gave her her father's
wife's phone number.


00:16:16.404 --> 00:16:17.739
You know what?


00:16:17.822 --> 00:16:19.657
Let's get you back to bed. You're tired.


00:16:19.741 --> 00:16:21.117
Yeah, but I have to tell you this.


00:16:21.201 --> 00:16:23.369
We can... We can talk more later.


00:16:24.412 --> 00:16:26.372
So, one day...


00:16:28.833 --> 00:16:31.586
- I got a call from Fred's wife.
- Okay.


00:16:31.669 --> 00:16:33.338
And she told me


00:16:33.421 --> 00:16:35.590
- that she wanted an address.
- Mm-hm.


00:16:35.673 --> 00:16:37.258
She wanted to send me something.


00:16:37.342 --> 00:16:38.593
Mm-hm.


00:16:38.676 --> 00:16:40.136
And, shortly after,


00:16:41.095 --> 00:16:44.182
I received a note in the mail and a letter


00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:47.977
that the wife received from Michelle,


00:16:49.229 --> 00:16:50.563
introducing herself


00:16:51.147 --> 00:16:53.024
and saying that it was her,


00:16:53.816 --> 00:16:54.901
Fred's daughter,


00:16:55.527 --> 00:16:57.820
who had been in the burning house.


00:16:59.113 --> 00:17:01.533
"It was me he tried to save."


00:17:02.408 --> 00:17:05.912
"It was me for whom he died..."


00:17:06.829 --> 00:17:09.374
That's what Michelle said to the wife.


00:17:09.457 --> 00:17:10.875
That's insane!


00:17:10.959 --> 00:17:11.960
Yes.


00:17:19.926 --> 00:17:21.302
Hi!


00:17:21.386 --> 00:17:23.155
<i>It's Martha, the nuisance.</i>


00:17:23.179 --> 00:17:25.056
You're not a nuisance.


00:17:25.139 --> 00:17:26.599
How're you feeling?


00:17:26.683 --> 00:17:28.268
<i>Fine. I'm at home.</i>


00:17:28.351 --> 00:17:32.480
The hospital's given me a few days off
between treatments, so I'm at home.


00:17:32.564 --> 00:17:34.065
I'd love for you to come over.


00:17:34.607 --> 00:17:37.443
Ooh, you've caught me
in the middle of moving.


00:17:37.527 --> 00:17:39.571
Oh, then you're really busy, right?


00:17:40.321 --> 00:17:43.324
Um, well, you know what moving's like.


00:17:43.408 --> 00:17:47.579
But, um, if you're feeling lonely,
I could stop by,


00:17:47.662 --> 00:17:49.247
we could take a walk in the park.


00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:51.249
I might not be quite up for a walk.


00:17:51.874 --> 00:17:54.961
Um, okay, you know what? Let me, um...


00:17:55.044 --> 00:17:58.631
Let me finish what I'm doing
and I'll be right over.


00:17:58.715 --> 00:18:01.926
Thanks, sweetheart,
but don't feel obliged.


00:18:26.367 --> 00:18:28.453
- These are for you.
- You are a darling.


00:18:29.746 --> 00:18:33.041
- And I've brought you a couple of books.
- Oh! Thank you.


00:18:33.124 --> 00:18:34.334
You want something to drink?


00:18:34.417 --> 00:18:36.586
Oh. I'd love some tea.


00:18:36.669 --> 00:18:38.880
- Herbal tea if you have it.
- Sure.


00:18:38.963 --> 00:18:40.965
- I'll put these in a vase.
- Okay.


00:18:42.258 --> 00:18:44.761
And all of this is for you.


00:18:44.844 --> 00:18:46.304
You have to finish all of it.


00:18:46.387 --> 00:18:48.640
Wow! Well, I will do my best.


00:18:48.723 --> 00:18:50.266
I love fruit.


00:18:54.354 --> 00:18:55.897
Are you working on something new?


00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:57.857
Um, yeah, actually I am.


00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.985
I'm doing research
on the painter Dora Carrington


00:19:01.069 --> 00:19:02.987
and her, um... Mm


00:19:03.613 --> 00:19:06.324
intense relationship with
the writer Lytton Strachey.


00:19:06.407 --> 00:19:07.992
- Mm-hm.
- Here he is.


00:19:08.534 --> 00:19:09.994
Uh, Strachey was gay,


00:19:10.078 --> 00:19:14.374
so she married the straight man
that he was infatuated with.


00:19:15.458 --> 00:19:17.251
It's gonna be the story of the trio.


00:19:17.335 --> 00:19:20.588
It isn't groundbreaking,
but I want to see where it takes me.


00:19:20.672 --> 00:19:22.215
Here, um, look.


00:19:22.298 --> 00:19:23.591
Um, unfortunately for her,


00:19:23.675 --> 00:19:26.177
there was another
more famous painter...


00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:27.679
- Leonora Carrington. Yeah.
- Yes,


00:19:27.762 --> 00:19:29.430
the surrealist Leonora Carrington,


00:19:29.514 --> 00:19:31.516
whose name was obviously
very similar to hers.


00:19:32.725 --> 00:19:33.810
Um...


00:19:34.519 --> 00:19:35.603
Dora


00:19:36.562 --> 00:19:38.523
was better known for this


00:19:38.606 --> 00:19:40.900
bizarre love story with Strachey.


00:19:43.194 --> 00:19:46.114
She devoted 17 years of her life to him.


00:19:46.197 --> 00:19:47.323
- Wow.
- Mm.


00:19:47.407 --> 00:19:49.200
It'll be a fictionalized biography, so...


00:19:50.034 --> 00:19:51.744
I'll make some stuff up, too.


00:19:53.079 --> 00:19:56.332
I've never been able to allow myself that.


00:19:57.083 --> 00:19:59.961
Mm. Well, I hope not.


00:20:00.044 --> 00:20:01.254
You're a war reporter.


00:20:01.921 --> 00:20:03.506
Yeah, you have to...


00:20:04.048 --> 00:20:05.608
You know, you can't show your emotions.


00:20:05.675 --> 00:20:09.595
You have to block them out
so you can do your job


00:20:09.679 --> 00:20:12.306
and stay in the present
in the middle of whatever hell.


00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:14.851
Maybe I should write about you
and not Carrington.


00:20:14.934 --> 00:20:18.187
I don't think you'd enjoy
writing about illnesses and treatments.


00:20:18.271 --> 00:20:20.606
- Mm. You're wrong.
- I'm just a journalist,


00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:23.234
addicted to wars and adrenaline.


00:20:24.026 --> 00:20:25.111
You think that's nothing?


00:20:27.447 --> 00:20:29.073
It wasn't all tragedy.


00:20:29.157 --> 00:20:30.533
You know, life went on.


00:20:32.618 --> 00:20:35.955
There was one report
when I added a bit of fiction.


00:20:36.539 --> 00:20:39.834
- Really?
- Actually, I never published it.


00:20:41.836 --> 00:20:43.796
It was during the war in Iraq.


00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:47.258
<i>On the last day, before we left Baghdad.</i>


00:20:47.341 --> 00:20:49.010
Are you sure this is the right way?


00:20:49.093 --> 00:20:51.888
Yeah, just make a left here in this alley.


00:20:53.222 --> 00:20:54.474
Let's make this brief.


00:20:57.977 --> 00:20:59.061
Here. Stop here.


00:21:09.322 --> 00:21:11.991
Martin, what are you doing
here in Baghdad?


00:21:14.202 --> 00:21:15.661
You look great. You really do.


00:21:15.745 --> 00:21:16.746
Thank you.


00:21:16.829 --> 00:21:18.748
Yeah, I'm sorry. Paco, Martin.


00:21:18.831 --> 00:21:20.166
He's a Carmelite, like me.


00:21:20.249 --> 00:21:22.168
Pleasure. Let me introduce you
to Martha.


00:21:22.251 --> 00:21:24.545
She is a brilliant journalist
from <i>The New York Times.</i>


00:21:26.005 --> 00:21:27.816
They are the Carmelites
I was telling you about.


00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:29.160
It's a pleasure to meet you both.


00:21:29.634 --> 00:21:31.260
Are you intending to stay in Baghdad?


00:21:31.803 --> 00:21:33.095
Yes, here we are.


00:21:33.179 --> 00:21:34.180
But you're alone.


00:21:34.847 --> 00:21:37.141
All the NGOs and the Red Cross
have left already.


00:21:37.767 --> 00:21:39.060
I know.


00:21:39.143 --> 00:21:42.355
The situation is out of control.
It's very dangerous.


00:21:42.438 --> 00:21:43.439
You're here as well.


00:21:43.523 --> 00:21:44.792
Yeah, but we're just passing through.


00:21:44.816 --> 00:21:47.360
We're leaving as soon as
we finish talking to you.


00:21:47.443 --> 00:21:49.195
We can't let them down now,


00:21:49.278 --> 00:21:50.758
this is when the people need us most.


00:21:50.822 --> 00:21:54.617
That's true, but it's still
extremely dangerous.


00:21:56.285 --> 00:21:57.328
But then you know that.


00:21:58.079 --> 00:22:00.206
We can't let them down now, <i>señora.</i>


00:22:01.624 --> 00:22:03.209
Do you mind if we take a photo of you


00:22:03.292 --> 00:22:05.127
and how the mission has been left?


00:22:06.587 --> 00:22:07.880
Okay.


00:22:07.964 --> 00:22:10.216
You can photograph the mission and me,


00:22:10.299 --> 00:22:13.636
but he doesn't want to risk
his family in Spain seeing him.


00:22:13.719 --> 00:22:15.030
- They'd worry.
- Yeah, of course.


00:22:15.054 --> 00:22:17.741
Totally understand, but if we could
get one of you, that would be great.


00:22:17.765 --> 00:22:19.183
- Okay.
- Sure.


00:22:20.393 --> 00:22:21.753
- Here?
- Yeah.


00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:25.314
Just perhaps a little tiny step closer...


00:22:25.398 --> 00:22:27.209
Yeah, that's fine,
so that I can see the impacts.


00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:34.073
I think you have it.


00:22:36.659 --> 00:22:37.702
How long has it been


00:22:38.661 --> 00:22:39.996
since we last saw each other?


00:22:40.079 --> 00:22:41.122
Five years.


00:22:41.747 --> 00:22:42.999
Five years.


00:22:44.125 --> 00:22:45.167
Wow.


00:22:46.544 --> 00:22:47.628
Do you remember Liberia?


00:22:48.546 --> 00:22:49.672
How could I forget?


00:22:51.799 --> 00:22:54.218
Look, I have some photos of you
that we didn't publish.


00:22:55.636 --> 00:22:57.597
If you give me an address,
I can send them to you.


00:22:57.680 --> 00:22:58.681
Maybe to the Embassy.


00:22:58.764 --> 00:22:59.849
No, you keep them.


00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:02.351
That way I'll keep you company.


00:23:03.477 --> 00:23:04.477
Okay.


00:23:06.898 --> 00:23:08.274
It was really great seeing you.


00:23:09.150 --> 00:23:09.984
Take care.


00:23:10.067 --> 00:23:11.485
- Goodbye.
- Be safe.


00:23:16.282 --> 00:23:17.617
How do you know the Carmelite?


00:23:20.870 --> 00:23:21.913
We met in Sierra Leone.


00:23:24.206 --> 00:23:25.416
We became lovers there.


00:23:26.167 --> 00:23:27.793
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.


00:23:29.086 --> 00:23:30.630
After that, we met more times.


00:23:31.255 --> 00:23:33.633
Always in places that were at war.


00:23:33.716 --> 00:23:34.967
And you had sex?


00:23:35.051 --> 00:23:37.470
Well, of course, yeah.


00:23:37.553 --> 00:23:39.639
Bernardo never renounced
physical pleasure.


00:23:41.140 --> 00:23:43.351
He was always in
the most conflictive places.


00:23:44.018 --> 00:23:46.270
And I think that sex was his best shield.


00:23:48.731 --> 00:23:51.108
I'm pretty sure
the Carmelite is his partner.


00:23:51.192 --> 00:23:52.318
You think so?


00:23:52.401 --> 00:23:53.444
Definitely.


00:23:54.654 --> 00:23:56.256
That is the only way
you can stay in Baghdad


00:23:56.280 --> 00:23:57.440
and not be afraid of the war.


00:23:58.658 --> 00:24:00.868
- What a wonderful story.
- Yup.


00:24:02.912 --> 00:24:03.913
Don't you dare write it.


00:24:03.996 --> 00:24:06.040
No, no, no, of course not.


00:24:08.918 --> 00:24:11.087
But how about sin for him?


00:24:11.921 --> 00:24:13.161
I mean, don't they feel guilty?


00:24:13.214 --> 00:24:14.548
After all, they are Catholic.


00:24:15.091 --> 00:24:17.051
Yeah, I don't know.
He never talked about that.


00:24:19.220 --> 00:24:20.930
With all the horrors you see in war,


00:24:21.931 --> 00:24:24.642
feeling guilty about having sex
doesn't really carry much weight,


00:24:26.018 --> 00:24:27.061
you simply get used to it.


00:24:28.229 --> 00:24:29.313
I know that.


00:24:32.733 --> 00:24:34.402
I wrote their story,


00:24:34.485 --> 00:24:36.821
their love story, as I imagined it,


00:24:38.072 --> 00:24:39.657
but it stayed in my computer.


00:24:41.867 --> 00:24:46.163
So, you're gonna write about
Dora Carrington's insane love.


00:24:46.247 --> 00:24:48.874
Mm-hm.
And her connection to Virginia Woolf,


00:24:48.958 --> 00:24:52.169
who Strachey also pursued romantically.


00:24:52.253 --> 00:24:53.671
What a group!


00:24:53.754 --> 00:24:55.715
I so admire their freedom.


00:24:56.257 --> 00:24:57.925
Strachey died of stomach cancer


00:24:58.009 --> 00:25:00.219
18 years after meeting Dora


00:25:00.302 --> 00:25:03.097
and Dora survived him
by barely two months


00:25:03.180 --> 00:25:05.391
before she shot herself in the stomach.


00:25:05.474 --> 00:25:06.892
She was only 38.


00:25:08.144 --> 00:25:10.730
I'm struck by the symmetry
of that kind of gesture,


00:25:11.272 --> 00:25:12.440
his stomach cancer


00:25:12.523 --> 00:25:14.650
and her shooting herself in the stomach.


00:25:14.734 --> 00:25:16.402
I know, it struck me, too.


00:25:17.153 --> 00:25:20.740
I wonder what Virginia Woolf
thought of Carrington's death?


00:25:21.532 --> 00:25:23.409
Maybe Virginia saw


00:25:24.118 --> 00:25:25.286
a kind of warning,


00:25:25.369 --> 00:25:27.955
a mirror that reflected her?


00:25:28.039 --> 00:25:29.039
As if they were fated?


00:25:31.834 --> 00:25:33.794
Do you think I'm fated, too?


00:25:33.878 --> 00:25:36.630
No! Of course not.


00:25:36.714 --> 00:25:39.216
I've never known anyone
more alive than you.


00:25:39.300 --> 00:25:41.886
This week I'm starting
a new experimental


00:25:41.969 --> 00:25:44.180
- immunotherapy treatment.
- Uh-huh.


00:25:44.263 --> 00:25:45.306
They've already tried it


00:25:45.389 --> 00:25:48.100
and it seems to work well
with cases of cervical cancer.


00:25:48.184 --> 00:25:50.019
- Well, that's great news!
- Yeah.


00:25:50.978 --> 00:25:52.330
Let me know
when I can come and visit you,


00:25:52.354 --> 00:25:53.522
- okay?
- I will.


00:25:55.858 --> 00:25:58.277
- Talking of symmetry...
- Mm-hmm?


00:25:58.360 --> 00:25:59.403
Do you remember...


00:26:00.446 --> 00:26:01.655
Damian Cunningham?


00:26:02.698 --> 00:26:04.533
How can I forget?


00:26:04.617 --> 00:26:07.161
I inherited him from you.


00:26:07.244 --> 00:26:08.954
The shared lover.


00:26:09.038 --> 00:26:10.498
- Well, I...
- I have to say


00:26:10.581 --> 00:26:12.291
I felt terrible when you got together


00:26:12.374 --> 00:26:13.667
after I'd been with him.


00:26:13.751 --> 00:26:16.146
Okay, we didn't share him exactly
because you'd already broken up


00:26:16.170 --> 00:26:17.230
and you were out of the country.


00:26:17.254 --> 00:26:18.756
I would never go back with him


00:26:18.839 --> 00:26:21.342
and, to tell the truth,
I was never faithful.


00:26:22.259 --> 00:26:27.056
But he was a passionate
and enthusiastic lover


00:26:27.139 --> 00:26:29.183
and I hope he was for you, too.


00:26:29.266 --> 00:26:30.351
I had no complaints.


00:26:46.075 --> 00:26:47.076
Hi.


00:26:49.745 --> 00:26:50.746
What is it?


00:26:52.790 --> 00:26:53.791
It hasn't worked.


00:26:55.042 --> 00:26:57.086
I've got metastases in my liver


00:26:57.169 --> 00:26:59.046
- and in my bones.
- Oh, Martha.


00:26:59.130 --> 00:27:01.048
I should have followed my first instinct.


00:27:01.132 --> 00:27:03.717
Should never have put myself
through this torture.


00:27:03.801 --> 00:27:06.262
This diarrhea, vomiting, fatigue


00:27:06.345 --> 00:27:07.805
to end up like this.


00:27:08.597 --> 00:27:10.724
I should never have given in
to false hopes.


00:27:10.808 --> 00:27:12.059
Okay. Okay.


00:27:12.143 --> 00:27:14.061
All right, what does the doctor say?


00:27:14.145 --> 00:27:15.354
Tell me.


00:27:15.437 --> 00:27:17.356
Oh, that I could live for months,


00:27:17.982 --> 00:27:18.983
maybe a year.


00:27:19.984 --> 00:27:22.111
He wants me to continue
with the treatment,


00:27:22.194 --> 00:27:23.696
even though it looks hopeless.


00:27:23.779 --> 00:27:25.197
Maybe it will work this time.


00:27:25.281 --> 00:27:27.283
I don't wanna wallow in self-pity.


00:27:33.372 --> 00:27:36.125
But I'm not a stoic. I'm sorry.


00:27:36.208 --> 00:27:38.878
I don't wanna go through
excruciating pain.


00:27:40.421 --> 00:27:42.882
You can't be self-possessed
if you're in agony.


00:27:43.799 --> 00:27:45.176
You can't think straight.


00:27:45.926 --> 00:27:47.636
You can only think of one thing


00:27:47.720 --> 00:27:49.096
the fucking cancer.


00:27:51.974 --> 00:27:53.559
I've always taken care of my health,


00:27:54.560 --> 00:27:55.811
now I regret it.


00:27:56.562 --> 00:27:58.230
The doctor says I have a strong heart.


00:27:58.314 --> 00:27:59.523
What does that mean?


00:27:59.607 --> 00:28:01.400
My body is just gonna go on fighting


00:28:01.942 --> 00:28:04.904
while I suffer and suffer
until my last breath?


00:28:06.113 --> 00:28:07.198
I don't know.


00:28:09.158 --> 00:28:10.701
I don't know how to help you.


00:28:12.119 --> 00:28:13.204
I'm so sorry.


00:28:17.958 --> 00:28:20.419
I think I deserve a good death.


00:28:23.047 --> 00:28:25.883
At least one without convulsions
in my last moments.


00:28:26.717 --> 00:28:28.636
Going out with a little bit of dignity,


00:28:28.719 --> 00:28:30.304
clean and dry.


00:28:33.057 --> 00:28:35.392
But I know I'm asking too much...


00:28:35.476 --> 00:28:36.828
What are you doing up, Martha?


00:28:36.852 --> 00:28:38.520
I'm fucking over this.


00:28:39.271 --> 00:28:41.148
- Can you help her, please?
- Of course.


00:28:41.232 --> 00:28:42.483
Let's get you back in bed.


00:28:42.566 --> 00:28:44.568
Come on. Let me help you.


00:28:45.945 --> 00:28:46.987
Bring it on.


00:28:47.571 --> 00:28:48.614
Here we go.


00:28:51.533 --> 00:28:53.535
I'll end up turning into a junkie.


00:28:54.912 --> 00:28:56.872
I am one already, I guess.


00:28:56.956 --> 00:28:59.708
It's okay. Really.


00:28:59.792 --> 00:29:01.794
Here, this will help.


00:29:40.124 --> 00:29:41.166
Are you still here?


00:29:42.668 --> 00:29:43.669
Yes.


00:29:47.131 --> 00:29:49.049
Should I ask them to bring your dinner?


00:29:50.467 --> 00:29:51.468
Are you hungry?


00:29:52.219 --> 00:29:53.220
No.


00:29:56.307 --> 00:29:57.308
Ingrid...


00:29:59.727 --> 00:30:01.854
Do you think I need to say goodbye


00:30:01.937 --> 00:30:03.314
to my closest friends?


00:30:03.939 --> 00:30:06.191
I think you should do
whatever you wanna do.


00:30:07.318 --> 00:30:09.820
I just want peace and quiet.


00:30:11.655 --> 00:30:14.908
Have you thought about
how you wanna spend your time?


00:30:16.952 --> 00:30:17.953
And where?


00:30:18.787 --> 00:30:20.456
Is there some place you'd like to go?


00:30:21.665 --> 00:30:22.666
Look.


00:30:28.213 --> 00:30:29.798
Pink snowflakes.


00:30:32.259 --> 00:30:35.387
There had to be something good
about climate change.


00:30:37.598 --> 00:30:38.640
Well...


00:30:40.267 --> 00:30:41.894
I've lived to see that.


00:30:46.940 --> 00:30:49.902
You remember the end
of Joyce's <i>The Dead?</i>


00:30:49.985 --> 00:30:51.695
Vaguely.


00:30:53.155 --> 00:30:54.907
"The snow was falling,"


00:30:56.617 --> 00:30:59.078
falling on the lonely churchyard,


00:31:00.287 --> 00:31:03.248
falling faintly through the universe.


00:31:05.501 --> 00:31:07.461
And faintly falling,


00:31:08.212 --> 00:31:11.340
like the descent of their last end,


00:31:13.467 --> 00:31:18.222
"on all the living and the dead."


00:31:22.726 --> 00:31:24.269
It's getting late and, uh...


00:31:25.562 --> 00:31:26.563
I should be going.


00:31:34.613 --> 00:31:35.614
Thank you.


00:31:37.199 --> 00:31:38.742
I'll see you tomorrow.


00:32:25.831 --> 00:32:28.542
There's still a half an hour
before the movie starts.


00:32:28.625 --> 00:32:30.794
Should we go in and get
our seats before the rush?


00:32:30.878 --> 00:32:32.921
No. I wanna talk to you about something.


00:32:33.672 --> 00:32:34.590
Okay.


00:32:34.673 --> 00:32:37.009
I will not go out in mortifying anguish.


00:32:37.759 --> 00:32:39.511
I've gotten hold of a euthanasia pill.


00:32:40.345 --> 00:32:41.472
Don't ask me how,


00:32:41.555 --> 00:32:43.849
on the dark web
you can find almost anything.


00:32:44.475 --> 00:32:47.936
I also have an abundance of opioids
for the moments of pain.


00:32:48.020 --> 00:32:49.247
And don't look at me like that,


00:32:49.271 --> 00:32:51.607
I'm not asking you
to convince me otherwise.


00:32:52.524 --> 00:32:53.859
I don't know what to say.


00:32:54.651 --> 00:32:55.986
I'm hoping you'll say yes.


00:32:57.029 --> 00:32:58.030
Yes to what?


00:32:58.655 --> 00:33:00.365
To my asking you to help me.


00:33:01.074 --> 00:33:02.451
Help you what?


00:33:03.744 --> 00:33:07.831
I've faced death several times,
but I've always been accompanied.


00:33:08.707 --> 00:33:12.044
We reporters formed
a kind of mobile family.


00:33:13.962 --> 00:33:15.547
This is another war,


00:33:16.590 --> 00:33:17.883
I'm not afraid of it.


00:33:18.425 --> 00:33:19.635
But


00:33:19.718 --> 00:33:21.803
like the other times I faced death...


00:33:23.722 --> 00:33:25.724
I don't wanna be alone, Ingrid.


00:33:28.227 --> 00:33:29.603
I'm asking you


00:33:30.521 --> 00:33:32.564
to be in the next room.


00:33:33.982 --> 00:33:35.651
I think we should go get our seats.


00:33:35.734 --> 00:33:38.487
Yeah, sure,
but I prefer to go on talking to you,


00:33:38.570 --> 00:33:39.738
if you don't mind.


00:33:42.324 --> 00:33:43.784
Okay. Um...


00:33:45.827 --> 00:33:47.329
Do you know when you wanna do this?


00:33:48.288 --> 00:33:49.289
Not exactly.


00:33:50.332 --> 00:33:51.333
Within a month?


00:33:53.418 --> 00:33:56.463
Before I start to deteriorate
and you don't recognize me.


00:33:57.548 --> 00:34:00.717
These next weeks
I should be reasonably well,


00:34:01.510 --> 00:34:03.220
but I wanna do it soon.


00:34:03.303 --> 00:34:06.890
My doctors think that I'm gonna return
to complete the treatment.


00:34:07.641 --> 00:34:10.018
It's best they don't suspect anything.


00:34:10.936 --> 00:34:12.771
Where do you wanna do it?


00:34:12.854 --> 00:34:14.147
I don't wanna be at home.


00:34:16.608 --> 00:34:19.570
And I don't wanna go back
to anywhere I've been happy.


00:34:22.030 --> 00:34:25.867
It's always a mistake to return
to some place you've been truly happy.


00:34:25.951 --> 00:34:28.412
You just ruin the good memories
of the first time.


00:34:28.495 --> 00:34:30.163
No, I understand that.


00:34:30.247 --> 00:34:33.458
I think it will be easier
for me to let myself go


00:34:33.542 --> 00:34:37.671
if I'm not surrounded by familiar things,


00:34:37.754 --> 00:34:38.922
intimate things.


00:34:39.715 --> 00:34:41.758
I think that would hold me back.


00:34:44.303 --> 00:34:47.306
I prefer some unknown place,


00:34:48.348 --> 00:34:50.142
comfortable and safe,


00:34:51.184 --> 00:34:52.811
and not too far away.


00:34:53.687 --> 00:34:55.856
Do you need my help finding a place


00:34:55.939 --> 00:34:58.150
or getting you settled in?


00:34:58.233 --> 00:34:59.693
No, no, no.


00:35:00.444 --> 00:35:01.945
No, I can take care of that part.


00:35:03.697 --> 00:35:06.575
What I need is somebody
to be there with me,


00:35:07.784 --> 00:35:09.244
in the room next door.


00:35:11.788 --> 00:35:13.707
Wouldn't you prefer
someone you're closer to?


00:35:13.790 --> 00:35:15.125
We're very close.


00:35:15.208 --> 00:35:17.252
No, yes, of course, of course we are.


00:35:17.336 --> 00:35:19.671
Oh, my God,
we're very close. I just...


00:35:19.755 --> 00:35:21.798
There were years where
we didn't see each other.


00:35:22.966 --> 00:35:24.468
What about Stella?


00:35:24.551 --> 00:35:25.844
Or Maggie?


00:35:25.927 --> 00:35:26.928
Or Vanessa?


00:35:27.012 --> 00:35:29.097
You've all been friends
since you were kids.


00:35:29.181 --> 00:35:31.516
I admit I thought of them first.


00:35:32.559 --> 00:35:34.269
I asked all three of them.


00:35:34.353 --> 00:35:37.648
They all were horrified
and they all said no.


00:35:38.982 --> 00:35:40.067
They understood it,


00:35:40.150 --> 00:35:42.361
but they said they could never be a part


00:35:42.444 --> 00:35:44.321
of helping me take my own life.


00:35:44.404 --> 00:35:45.947
Absolutely not.


00:35:46.031 --> 00:35:48.271
- What about your daughter?
- It wouldn't be fair to her.


00:35:49.660 --> 00:35:51.161
I've been an absent mother.


00:35:51.787 --> 00:35:53.580
I don't wanna impose my dying on her.


00:35:53.664 --> 00:35:57.876
You could at least consult her
and let her be a part of it.


00:35:57.959 --> 00:35:59.670
We're two strangers, Ingrid.


00:36:01.380 --> 00:36:05.092
She made that clear when I told her
about my doubts about the treatment.


00:36:06.218 --> 00:36:07.886
"It's your choice," she said.


00:36:09.680 --> 00:36:10.806
And she's right.


00:36:11.390 --> 00:36:12.391
Right.


00:36:39.126 --> 00:36:40.585
No matter what,


00:36:41.378 --> 00:36:43.547
people want you to keep fighting.


00:36:45.257 --> 00:36:48.009
This is the way we've
been taught to see cancer.


00:36:49.136 --> 00:36:53.724
As a fight... between patient and disease,


00:36:54.349 --> 00:36:56.810
which is to say between good and evil.


00:36:57.686 --> 00:36:59.813
If you survive, you're a hero.


00:37:00.939 --> 00:37:02.774
If you lose, well,


00:37:04.401 --> 00:37:06.194
perhaps you didn't fight hard enough.


00:37:08.780 --> 00:37:10.615
People don't like using words like


00:37:10.699 --> 00:37:13.869
"terminal" or "incurable."


00:37:13.952 --> 00:37:15.787
They call that defeatist talk.


00:37:16.621 --> 00:37:20.333
Some of the worst stuff comes from
the cancer support community.


00:37:21.042 --> 00:37:23.962
Some of them think
of your cancer as a gift,


00:37:24.045 --> 00:37:26.757
an opportunity for spiritual growth.


00:37:26.840 --> 00:37:27.924
Bullshit!


00:37:28.717 --> 00:37:31.803
People should see
this is my way of fighting.


00:37:33.972 --> 00:37:37.100
Cancer can't get me if I get me first.


00:37:39.853 --> 00:37:42.355
And what's the point in waiting


00:37:43.607 --> 00:37:44.941
when I'm so ready to go?


00:37:46.693 --> 00:37:48.945
Are you completely sure you're ready?


00:37:49.029 --> 00:37:50.071
Totally.


00:37:50.947 --> 00:37:52.282
Since the first diagnosis.


00:37:55.035 --> 00:37:57.454
You know I have a terrible fear of death.


00:37:57.537 --> 00:37:58.622
I know.


00:37:58.705 --> 00:38:00.040
I've read your book.


00:38:00.123 --> 00:38:01.958
That's why I didn't ask you first.


00:38:04.294 --> 00:38:05.462
But you understand me,


00:38:05.545 --> 00:38:06.838
- don't you?
- I do, I do.


00:38:06.922 --> 00:38:09.216
I envy you. You're in control of your life.


00:38:09.299 --> 00:38:12.844
I only need you to accompany me
the days leading to it,


00:38:12.928 --> 00:38:14.554
as if we were on vacation.


00:38:15.639 --> 00:38:18.308
I just wanna know that, when it happens,


00:38:18.391 --> 00:38:20.352
there'll be someone in the next room.


00:38:20.435 --> 00:38:21.937
It terrifies me, Martha.


00:38:22.020 --> 00:38:23.021
I understand.


00:38:23.104 --> 00:38:24.940
I think that you have
every right to do this


00:38:25.023 --> 00:38:26.066
and I admire you for it,


00:38:26.149 --> 00:38:28.568
but I don't know that I can be
the one to find you dead.


00:38:28.652 --> 00:38:29.736
I'm not that strong.


00:38:29.820 --> 00:38:31.696
You're much stronger
than you think you are.


00:38:34.324 --> 00:38:36.785
Anyway, I had to try.


00:38:40.831 --> 00:38:43.959
I can't answer you now, Martha,
but I promise you I'll think about it.


00:38:44.042 --> 00:38:46.711
Right now I'm too confused
and too terrified.


00:38:46.795 --> 00:38:48.338
I understand.


00:38:48.421 --> 00:38:50.173
I understand it's sudden,


00:38:52.259 --> 00:38:53.927
and it's disconcerting.


00:38:58.515 --> 00:38:59.516
I'll think of someone.


00:39:10.318 --> 00:39:11.403
I wasn't too much?


00:39:11.486 --> 00:39:12.863
No, no.


00:39:52.694 --> 00:39:53.528
Martha?


00:39:53.612 --> 00:39:54.881
<i>Hello, Ingrid.</i>


00:39:54.905 --> 00:39:56.239
I've made up my mind.


00:39:59.659 --> 00:40:00.659
Come on in.


00:40:01.912 --> 00:40:03.496
The owner is a jewelry designer.


00:40:04.247 --> 00:40:07.042
She is a friend of mine,
so I don't pay much rent.


00:40:07.125 --> 00:40:08.125
Mm.


00:40:08.793 --> 00:40:10.712
You get the impression
it's been furnished


00:40:10.795 --> 00:40:12.172
with stuff from the garbage.


00:40:12.797 --> 00:40:14.215
Not everything.


00:40:15.216 --> 00:40:17.844
And it takes talent to pick stuff
out of the garbage.


00:40:18.428 --> 00:40:19.971
You haven't finished moving in.


00:40:20.889 --> 00:40:21.932
Do you want a hand?


00:40:22.015 --> 00:40:23.016
Uh...


00:40:23.767 --> 00:40:24.976
No.


00:40:27.520 --> 00:40:28.521
I'll do it after.


00:40:30.023 --> 00:40:33.401
And, even so, you're going with Martha.


00:40:33.485 --> 00:40:36.696
She is totally alone, Damian.


00:40:37.447 --> 00:40:39.741
None of her friends
are helping her with this.


00:40:39.824 --> 00:40:41.910
She even told me
I wasn't her first choice.


00:40:43.036 --> 00:40:45.205
It's like her daughter doesn't even exist.


00:40:45.288 --> 00:40:46.408
In the years I was with her,


00:40:46.456 --> 00:40:48.333
she never told me she had a daughter.


00:40:48.416 --> 00:40:49.584
I know, it's a...


00:40:50.210 --> 00:40:51.586
It's a sad story.


00:40:51.670 --> 00:40:54.881
It's a terrible, terrible misunderstanding.


00:40:58.176 --> 00:41:00.095
Have you told her that we're in touch?


00:41:00.178 --> 00:41:01.680
Uh...


00:41:01.763 --> 00:41:02.806
No...


00:41:02.889 --> 00:41:05.433
Um, we've talked about you
in a... in a general way.


00:41:05.517 --> 00:41:07.519
- She has nice memories of you.
- Oh. Really?


00:41:08.603 --> 00:41:11.022
Our relationship was mostly physical.


00:41:11.106 --> 00:41:13.108
She was always about to go off
somewhere else,


00:41:13.900 --> 00:41:18.279
that's why our lovemaking
had that sense of urgency.


00:41:18.363 --> 00:41:20.657
It was like having sex with a terrorist


00:41:20.740 --> 00:41:22.158
it always felt like the last time.


00:41:22.242 --> 00:41:24.661
Well, she rates you
pretty highly as a lover.


00:41:24.744 --> 00:41:26.384
I'd like to know what rating you give me.


00:41:26.454 --> 00:41:28.540
Oh, I can't believe
you're still flirting with me.


00:41:28.623 --> 00:41:31.334
- I'm serious.
- No, no, you're not serious.


00:41:31.418 --> 00:41:33.503
What's serious is Martha's situation.


00:41:34.087 --> 00:41:35.880
And your being terrified of death?


00:41:36.589 --> 00:41:38.383
You just published a book about that.


00:41:38.466 --> 00:41:40.468
Have you overcome that
thanks to the book?


00:41:40.552 --> 00:41:42.721
No.


00:41:51.604 --> 00:41:53.898
Hi. How are you?


00:41:53.982 --> 00:41:55.316
Better.


00:41:55.400 --> 00:41:57.485
Much better since you said yes.


00:41:58.194 --> 00:41:59.863
Where are you? Are you at home?


00:41:59.946 --> 00:42:01.114
<i>Yeah.</i>


00:42:01.197 --> 00:42:02.741
I'm watering the plants.


00:42:02.824 --> 00:42:05.452
Oh, I thought you had someone
who did that for you.


00:42:05.535 --> 00:42:06.535
<i>I do.</i>


00:42:07.203 --> 00:42:09.831
But today I felt like doing it
and I am enjoying it.


00:42:09.914 --> 00:42:12.125
<i>Okay. Good.</i>


00:42:12.208 --> 00:42:15.795
Um, have you... Have you
decided where we're going?


00:42:16.337 --> 00:42:17.756
That's why I called.


00:42:18.757 --> 00:42:22.343
<i>It's, uh, near Woodstock,
it's about two hours from the city.</i>


00:42:22.427 --> 00:42:24.429
It looks fantastic. Uh...


00:42:24.512 --> 00:42:28.349
It's a bit expensive,
but, hey, the occasion calls for it.


00:42:30.435 --> 00:42:32.729
So, do you know how long...


00:42:32.812 --> 00:42:34.355
I've rented it for a month.


00:42:34.439 --> 00:42:36.941
That should give me
more than enough time.


00:42:37.025 --> 00:42:38.026
A month?


00:42:38.109 --> 00:42:41.154
<i>Yeah. My blood count's low</i>


00:42:41.237 --> 00:42:43.698
and I have to take a break
before I start the new treatment


00:42:43.782 --> 00:42:46.868
and you are the only one who knows
I'm not going back to the hospital.


00:42:47.494 --> 00:42:49.746
<i>It's not like I've picked a date.</i>


00:42:49.829 --> 00:42:50.705
<i>I mean,</i>


00:42:50.789 --> 00:42:52.749
you'll never know it anyway.


00:42:53.833 --> 00:42:56.127
But... I'm ready to go.


00:42:57.837 --> 00:42:59.589
I would even say I'm impatient.


00:43:00.548 --> 00:43:02.300
I'm gonna be giving a lecture


00:43:02.383 --> 00:43:04.385
near Woodstock at Bard in two weeks,


00:43:04.469 --> 00:43:05.720
so we can see each other.


00:43:05.804 --> 00:43:09.682
Mm, I don't think that's a good idea,
I'll be with Martha all the time.


00:43:10.350 --> 00:43:11.518
I'll call you if I can.


00:43:12.060 --> 00:43:13.260
You're going to need a lawyer.


00:43:13.770 --> 00:43:15.772
Yes, I should look for one.


00:43:15.855 --> 00:43:18.942
Let me help you with that,
but I'll have to fill them in.


00:43:19.025 --> 00:43:21.486
No, no, in that case, no.


00:43:21.569 --> 00:43:22.904
This is an absolute secret.


00:43:22.987 --> 00:43:24.572
Martha doesn't even know I've told you.


00:43:24.656 --> 00:43:27.659
Okay. But if you need anything,
you should let me know.


00:43:29.494 --> 00:43:30.829
I worry about you.


00:43:31.788 --> 00:43:32.788
Thank you.


00:44:30.972 --> 00:44:32.223
According to this map,


00:44:32.932 --> 00:44:34.976
we go up these stairs to enter the house.


00:44:35.059 --> 00:44:36.102
Okay.


00:45:05.965 --> 00:45:07.091
Look at this.


00:45:22.315 --> 00:45:24.609
Wow, it's so beautiful!


00:45:24.692 --> 00:45:27.946
It's so much more beautiful
than in the photographs!


00:45:31.699 --> 00:45:33.534
Is that a real Hopper?


00:45:33.618 --> 00:45:35.658
I don't think
they would have left it here.


00:45:36.287 --> 00:45:38.122
It's a very good copy.


00:45:38.206 --> 00:45:39.207
It looks real.


00:46:02.605 --> 00:46:04.399
- Do you hear them?
- Mm-hmm.


00:46:04.482 --> 00:46:05.692
Isn't that wonderful?


00:46:10.405 --> 00:46:13.324
And we can lie in the sun,
like in the Hopper,


00:46:14.993 --> 00:46:17.328
and catch the evening breeze.


00:46:22.959 --> 00:46:24.085
Are you okay?


00:46:26.546 --> 00:46:27.547
Very happy.


00:46:45.690 --> 00:46:47.358
Do you mind if I take this one?


00:46:47.442 --> 00:46:49.235
Of course not. It's your house.


00:46:52.947 --> 00:46:56.326
Mm. This one is a little small,
I'm gonna look downstairs.


00:46:56.409 --> 00:46:57.409
All right.


00:47:15.219 --> 00:47:17.180
I'm gonna take this one, okay?


00:47:18.139 --> 00:47:19.432
Very good!


00:47:21.017 --> 00:47:23.728
You don't mind that
I'm not in the room next door?


00:47:24.437 --> 00:47:26.439
I can hear you breathe!


00:47:27.357 --> 00:47:28.858
And yell!


00:47:28.941 --> 00:47:31.527
Okay!


00:47:39.744 --> 00:47:41.829
Here we go.


00:47:45.750 --> 00:47:47.585
Let's get you unpacked.


00:47:47.668 --> 00:47:48.669
Thank you.


00:47:49.545 --> 00:47:50.838
I'll unpack it later.


00:47:51.464 --> 00:47:53.674
You're not my caretaker, Ingrid.


00:47:53.758 --> 00:47:54.926
You're my guest.


00:47:55.676 --> 00:47:56.844
Okay.


00:47:56.928 --> 00:47:57.928
Um...


00:47:57.970 --> 00:47:59.639
I'll go unpack my things.


00:48:16.864 --> 00:48:18.449
- Martha?
- Aah!


00:48:24.038 --> 00:48:25.039
What is it, honey?


00:48:25.957 --> 00:48:27.375
- You won't believe it!
- What?


00:48:27.458 --> 00:48:28.543
I forgot it!


00:48:28.626 --> 00:48:30.086
You forgot what?


00:48:30.169 --> 00:48:31.546
The pill, the euthanasia pill!


00:48:31.629 --> 00:48:34.006
I brought all the others!
We have to go back.


00:48:34.090 --> 00:48:36.151
Oh, it's okay, we'll go back
first thing in the morning.


00:48:36.175 --> 00:48:37.486
- Don't worry about it.
- No, not tomorrow!


00:48:37.510 --> 00:48:38.886
We have to go now!


00:48:38.970 --> 00:48:42.765
I just need to be sure
that I didn't lose it or misplace it,


00:48:42.849 --> 00:48:44.809
that I didn't just dream it up.


00:48:45.643 --> 00:48:46.644
Okay.


00:48:52.442 --> 00:48:55.236
Buying another pill would be
extremely complicated.


00:48:57.488 --> 00:49:01.242
I have a friend
who knows a mathematician


00:49:01.325 --> 00:49:03.244
who found it on the dark web.


00:49:04.495 --> 00:49:05.830
It's all very sordid,


00:49:06.747 --> 00:49:09.000
not to mention totally illegal.


00:49:12.211 --> 00:49:13.296
It's scary


00:49:14.172 --> 00:49:15.715
knowing that all that exists


00:49:16.257 --> 00:49:18.468
just behind our computer screens.


00:49:20.928 --> 00:49:22.180
I feel like a criminal.


00:49:27.393 --> 00:49:29.020
I never thought I'd be back here again.


00:49:29.937 --> 00:49:31.355
With that wonderful skyline.


00:49:32.190 --> 00:49:34.442
Life always surprises you.


00:49:34.525 --> 00:49:36.027
All right, let's get to work.


00:49:36.110 --> 00:49:37.987
- Okay.
- I'll start in the kitchen.


00:49:38.070 --> 00:49:39.197
Don't worry, we'll find it.


00:49:39.280 --> 00:49:41.049
Just, um... Just try to think
of all the places


00:49:41.073 --> 00:49:42.450
you usually hide things.


00:49:42.533 --> 00:49:44.253
This is the first thing I have ever hidden.


00:49:44.285 --> 00:49:45.119
Really?


00:49:45.203 --> 00:49:47.872
The only thing I can remember
is I put it in an envelope.


00:49:48.498 --> 00:49:49.999
Okay. Uh...


00:49:50.082 --> 00:49:51.751
Why don't I start in your office?


00:49:51.834 --> 00:49:53.187
- Is that okay? Okay.
- Yeah, yeah.


00:49:53.211 --> 00:49:55.630
Where did I put it? Where did I put it?


00:50:14.607 --> 00:50:16.901
Oh, my God.
We're never gonna find it.


00:51:31.517 --> 00:51:32.643
I found an envelope.


00:51:33.519 --> 00:51:34.519
That's it!


00:51:35.354 --> 00:51:36.397
Where did you find it?


00:51:36.480 --> 00:51:37.648
In your desk.


00:51:37.732 --> 00:51:40.192
There was key in a drawer
and I opened it.


00:51:40.818 --> 00:51:42.903
How could I have forgotten?


00:51:42.987 --> 00:51:44.363
I even left the key in it?


00:51:44.447 --> 00:51:45.966
Well, you meant to take it,
at the last minute,


00:51:45.990 --> 00:51:47.783
you forgot. It's not so weird.


00:51:50.286 --> 00:51:51.495
Thank you.


00:51:52.496 --> 00:51:54.457
Such a strange sensation.


00:51:55.916 --> 00:51:57.793
It's like being here after I'm dead.


00:51:57.877 --> 00:51:59.295
Oh, God, don't say that.


00:52:00.212 --> 00:52:02.715
It's too soon for you
to refer to yourself as a ghost.


00:52:04.300 --> 00:52:06.093
Let me straighten up before we leave.


00:52:06.177 --> 00:52:07.177
Thank you.


00:53:02.441 --> 00:53:03.943
Forgive me for all this hassle.


00:53:04.777 --> 00:53:06.028
I'm sorry, really.


00:53:06.112 --> 00:53:07.613
It's okay.


00:53:08.781 --> 00:53:11.158
What a great place to return to.


00:53:12.785 --> 00:53:14.203
Stupid fridge.


00:53:15.121 --> 00:53:16.163
You need some help?


00:53:18.958 --> 00:53:19.958
I got it.


00:53:27.049 --> 00:53:28.092
You know, maybe


00:53:29.051 --> 00:53:31.470
leaving the pill behind
was a kind of a sign?


00:53:33.305 --> 00:53:35.224
Maybe you're not as ready as you think.


00:53:37.768 --> 00:53:40.020
I told you never to say that to me.


00:53:41.897 --> 00:53:43.482
I don't remember you telling me that.


00:53:46.485 --> 00:53:48.446
I think I've said so many things to you.


00:53:49.989 --> 00:53:51.991
That's the problem with chemo brain.


00:53:53.743 --> 00:53:57.079
My memory keeps failing me
and I get distracted so easily.


00:53:59.498 --> 00:54:03.002
It can continue even
after the treatment stops


00:54:03.085 --> 00:54:04.754
and it can go on for years.


00:54:05.880 --> 00:54:07.590
I'll be spared that, at least.


00:54:10.509 --> 00:54:11.510
When I write


00:54:12.970 --> 00:54:13.971
when I wrote...


00:54:15.931 --> 00:54:18.684
I had to proofread a thousand times.


00:54:18.768 --> 00:54:21.270
I can't trust my judgement
about anything anymore.


00:54:21.353 --> 00:54:22.354
Well...


00:54:23.189 --> 00:54:25.775
Then why do you trust this decision?


00:54:26.650 --> 00:54:28.861
How do you know
it's not chemo brain, too?


00:54:30.696 --> 00:54:33.824
I've left the pill in the top drawer
of the bedside table.


00:54:34.909 --> 00:54:37.912
If I forget, which I don't think I will,


00:54:37.995 --> 00:54:38.996
you will remind me.


00:54:40.206 --> 00:54:42.708
And I prefer not to talk
about this anymore.


00:54:43.542 --> 00:54:46.337
Well, it's my business, too,
don't you think?


00:54:49.924 --> 00:54:51.342
Sure. Of course.


00:54:53.803 --> 00:54:56.138
I'll leave a signed letter for the police


00:54:56.222 --> 00:54:59.475
telling them everything,
including the name of the pill


00:54:59.558 --> 00:55:00.601
and where I got it.


00:55:01.477 --> 00:55:04.271
Your name will not appear anywhere.


00:55:05.397 --> 00:55:08.609
All you have to do is to say
that you know nothing.


00:55:09.235 --> 00:55:10.653
Don't budge from that.


00:55:12.029 --> 00:55:14.031
I don't wanna give you
any more information.


00:55:14.114 --> 00:55:15.449
The less you know, the better.


00:55:17.618 --> 00:55:18.786
And this is important.


00:55:25.042 --> 00:55:27.336
I'll sleep with my door open


00:55:27.419 --> 00:55:29.630
and the day that you find it closed


00:55:30.464 --> 00:55:32.174
is the day it's already happened.


00:55:33.050 --> 00:55:35.135
That's the sign, door closed.


00:55:41.100 --> 00:55:42.810
I know it's difficult.


00:55:45.646 --> 00:55:47.481
But just think we're on vacation.


00:55:49.191 --> 00:55:52.111
You can write, we can come and go...


00:55:53.195 --> 00:55:54.875
I don't think I'll be able to concentrate.


00:55:57.283 --> 00:55:58.701
And if I write,


00:55:58.784 --> 00:56:01.054
you might show up in it somewhere
and I don't wanna do that.


00:56:01.078 --> 00:56:02.162
Yeah.


00:56:02.246 --> 00:56:04.164
That could complicate your life


00:56:04.248 --> 00:56:06.041
if the police investigate.


00:56:06.125 --> 00:56:07.376
Well, I'm not gonna do it.


00:56:07.459 --> 00:56:08.752
Wait 'til I'm dead.


00:56:08.836 --> 00:56:09.837
Oh, God!


00:56:11.088 --> 00:56:14.592
Can you not say
"wait until I'm dead," please?


00:56:16.886 --> 00:56:17.886
I promise.


00:56:20.931 --> 00:56:22.492
I'd like to find a gym
somewhere around here


00:56:22.516 --> 00:56:24.156
that I can go to a couple of days a week.


00:56:26.437 --> 00:56:27.479
I'm the only one who eats


00:56:27.563 --> 00:56:29.857
and I don't want to gain ten pounds
while you waste away.


00:56:29.940 --> 00:56:31.442
Oh, give me a chance.


00:56:31.525 --> 00:56:32.693
I'll catch up with you.


00:56:36.447 --> 00:56:37.740
Look! I'm eating.


00:56:40.075 --> 00:56:42.620
<i>I have practically
held death in my hands.</i>


00:56:44.580 --> 00:56:47.541
<i>I never imagined it would be
something so light.</i>


00:57:23.702 --> 00:57:24.703
Martha?


00:57:29.166 --> 00:57:30.167
Good morning.


00:57:30.250 --> 00:57:31.293
Good morning!


00:57:32.002 --> 00:57:33.170
I'm making breakfast.


00:57:34.463 --> 00:57:35.547
You want some toast?


00:57:35.631 --> 00:57:37.466
No, just some coffee.


00:57:37.549 --> 00:57:38.884
Help yourself. It's already made.


00:57:38.968 --> 00:57:40.719
There's juice, fruit


00:57:41.387 --> 00:57:42.429
whatever you want.


00:57:48.227 --> 00:57:50.479
My behavior yesterday
was unacceptable.


00:57:51.605 --> 00:57:54.400
I completely understand
that it drove you crazy.


00:57:55.734 --> 00:57:56.986
But in my current state,


00:57:57.069 --> 00:57:59.071
I can't make any promises.


00:58:00.072 --> 00:58:01.240
So, just in case...


00:58:04.159 --> 00:58:06.870
I put a medium range sedative
in this drawer.


00:58:07.579 --> 00:58:09.206
And if you find me unbearable,


00:58:09.289 --> 00:58:12.751
you just have one and you can relax.


00:58:12.835 --> 00:58:14.211
I could have used that last night.


00:58:14.294 --> 00:58:16.046
You...


00:58:16.130 --> 00:58:18.549
You're one of a kind, Martha.
You really... You really are.


00:58:20.801 --> 00:58:22.720
I've made a list of stuff to buy.


00:58:22.803 --> 00:58:23.929
We need a few things.


00:58:25.639 --> 00:58:27.119
Is there anything you want me to get?


00:58:28.475 --> 00:58:29.560
Don't think so.


00:58:30.936 --> 00:58:32.456
Do you wanna come
to the store with me?


00:58:34.481 --> 00:58:35.607
Maybe another day.


00:58:36.275 --> 00:58:37.651
It's so nice here.


00:58:38.902 --> 00:58:41.113
I'd like to stay if you don't mind.


00:58:41.196 --> 00:58:42.448
No, of course not.


00:58:44.783 --> 00:58:47.286
I found a gym nearby, too.


00:58:47.911 --> 00:58:49.288
That's great.


00:58:49.371 --> 00:58:51.081
I think that's a very good idea.


00:58:54.376 --> 00:58:55.461
Okay, well...


00:58:57.046 --> 00:58:59.256
I have my phone with me
if you need anything.


00:59:00.090 --> 00:59:01.133
Thanks, love.


00:59:17.107 --> 00:59:17.941
Hi.


00:59:18.025 --> 00:59:19.818
I was hoping I could use the gym today.


00:59:19.902 --> 00:59:20.903
Are you a member?


00:59:20.986 --> 00:59:22.505
Uh, no. I'm just in town for a little bit.


00:59:22.529 --> 00:59:24.364
If you use one of our personal trainers,


00:59:24.448 --> 00:59:25.657
you don't need to be a member.


00:59:25.741 --> 00:59:28.202
Um, okay. I'll use
one of your trainers then.


00:59:28.285 --> 00:59:30.079
You'll like Jonah, you'll see.


00:59:30.996 --> 00:59:31.914
Thanks.


00:59:31.997 --> 00:59:34.875
So, would you like to start
a warm up doing steps?


00:59:34.958 --> 00:59:36.668
- Okay.
- Is okay?


00:59:36.752 --> 00:59:39.838
Do you think you can do this
for 30 seconds?


00:59:39.922 --> 00:59:42.549
- Um, sure. All right.
- Okay, go for it. Have a try.


00:59:43.634 --> 00:59:46.136
And we are on. Okay, nice.


00:59:46.220 --> 00:59:47.572
- Keep focus on your leg.
- Mm-hmm.


00:59:47.596 --> 00:59:49.139
And, if you can, move your arm...


00:59:49.223 --> 00:59:50.557
- Okay.
- Okay, with each step.


00:59:51.934 --> 00:59:52.935
And we are done.


00:59:53.644 --> 00:59:56.522
Nice. You're pretty strong,
you young lady.


00:59:56.605 --> 00:59:58.357
What I am is winded.


00:59:58.440 --> 01:00:01.026
Well, if you want,
there are other variations we can do.


01:00:02.486 --> 01:00:04.238
I mean, you can go try like this.


01:00:04.321 --> 01:00:05.614
You can go back and forth.


01:00:06.323 --> 01:00:08.992
Or you can jump on it and go left


01:00:09.076 --> 01:00:11.787
and right or back and on the box.


01:00:11.870 --> 01:00:13.580
- Okay. Okay.
- Have a try one more.


01:00:13.664 --> 01:00:15.916
Nice.


01:00:16.875 --> 01:00:18.269
- Focus on your core here.
- Uh-huh.


01:00:18.293 --> 01:00:19.503
And breathe.


01:00:21.088 --> 01:00:22.965
Inhale and exhale.


01:00:25.551 --> 01:00:26.635
Perfect. One more.


01:00:30.806 --> 01:00:31.849
Is everything okay?


01:00:37.187 --> 01:00:39.690
When the body is in great shape,
it takes longer to die.


01:00:42.734 --> 01:00:44.153
When death comes,


01:00:44.236 --> 01:00:46.738
the mind wants to go,
but the body keeps fighting.


01:00:47.573 --> 01:00:50.200
Heart beating "no" with every beat.


01:00:50.951 --> 01:00:51.952
Well


01:00:52.536 --> 01:00:54.496
all the more reason to look after yourself.


01:00:55.664 --> 01:00:57.082
I live with a friend who's dying.


01:00:57.166 --> 01:00:58.166
I'm sorry.


01:00:59.293 --> 01:01:01.211
Come. Let's have a seat.


01:01:01.795 --> 01:01:02.795
Come here.


01:01:07.134 --> 01:01:09.052
Is there anything that I can do?


01:01:15.350 --> 01:01:16.685
I wish I could give you a hug,


01:01:17.895 --> 01:01:19.897
but we're not allowed
to touch clients anymore


01:01:19.980 --> 01:01:22.232
because of the lawsuits and whatever.


01:01:25.527 --> 01:01:26.570
And it's a problem,


01:01:27.988 --> 01:01:29.841
because it can be hard
to correct people's posture


01:01:29.865 --> 01:01:30.991
with just words


01:01:31.742 --> 01:01:33.577
and touching is so important.


01:01:34.912 --> 01:01:36.914
This world is absurd and inhumane.


01:01:37.539 --> 01:01:39.833
I don't see it improving any time soon.


01:01:42.211 --> 01:01:43.754
But thank you, I feel hugged.


01:01:51.428 --> 01:01:53.972
Oh, I've been meaning to read this book.


01:01:54.723 --> 01:01:57.517
Isn't it a wonderful
title? <i>Erotic Vagrancy.</i>


01:01:57.601 --> 01:01:58.602
Do you wanna buy it?


01:02:00.896 --> 01:02:02.272
I won't have time to finish it.


01:02:09.696 --> 01:02:11.448
I like the way it's laid out here.


01:02:11.531 --> 01:02:12.532
Mm.


01:02:12.616 --> 01:02:13.659
Oh, look.


01:02:14.243 --> 01:02:15.494
Martha Gellhorn.


01:02:16.536 --> 01:02:18.038
<i>The View from the Ground.</i>


01:02:20.540 --> 01:02:24.211
She wrote that you only ever
truly love one war,


01:02:24.878 --> 01:02:26.838
after that you're just doing your duty.


01:02:29.091 --> 01:02:30.467
Which one was yours?


01:02:32.135 --> 01:02:34.054
Bosnia, without a doubt.


01:02:39.810 --> 01:02:42.604
The fight to survive
by the Bosnian people


01:02:42.688 --> 01:02:44.731
against a perfectly equipped army


01:02:45.732 --> 01:02:49.278
stole the hearts of all of us
who witnessed the extermination.


01:02:49.945 --> 01:02:52.823
There are very few women
war correspondents.


01:02:54.032 --> 01:02:55.826
War is a man's thing.


01:02:56.618 --> 01:02:58.745
You have to sort of become
one of the guys


01:02:58.829 --> 01:03:00.706
and it was never a problem for me,


01:03:00.789 --> 01:03:02.416
I've always lived like a man.


01:03:03.083 --> 01:03:07.129
Actually, I think
what Michelle really missed


01:03:08.046 --> 01:03:10.590
was having a maternal figure in her life.


01:03:11.550 --> 01:03:16.096
And in this, I must admit
that she... she was right.


01:03:16.888 --> 01:03:18.432
Don't be so hard on yourself.


01:03:23.520 --> 01:03:26.148
Hey, look who's coming to town!


01:03:26.231 --> 01:03:28.150
The life of the party!


01:03:28.233 --> 01:03:29.568
<i>"How bad can it get?</i>


01:03:30.235 --> 01:03:32.070
<i>Navigating urban life with integrity."</i>


01:03:32.154 --> 01:03:33.155
You feel like going?


01:03:33.238 --> 01:03:35.032
No, you know what? I've heard it already


01:03:35.115 --> 01:03:36.950
and it's not an evening I'd like to repeat.


01:03:37.034 --> 01:03:39.369
We all have
our own personal apocalypses.


01:03:39.453 --> 01:03:41.204
Are you having an awful time with me?


01:03:41.288 --> 01:03:43.915
No, no, I meant him, his lecture.


01:03:43.999 --> 01:03:45.792
Global crisis, climate change.


01:03:45.876 --> 01:03:47.169
Yeah.


01:03:47.252 --> 01:03:48.420
Hi.


01:03:48.503 --> 01:03:49.546
I love your hair.


01:03:50.213 --> 01:03:51.213
Nice.


01:04:02.309 --> 01:04:04.311
When the nightmares come rushing in,


01:04:05.437 --> 01:04:07.981
I think about all the men I've loved.


01:04:08.065 --> 01:04:09.566
It sounds like a song.


01:04:09.649 --> 01:04:11.526
A good one.


01:04:13.987 --> 01:04:15.947
Even if it was just for one night.


01:04:17.366 --> 01:04:20.160
Sometimes I think about Damian.


01:04:25.248 --> 01:04:29.669
I still think sex is the best way
to fend off looming thoughts of death.


01:04:31.254 --> 01:04:33.340
Like those Spanish Carmelites.


01:04:35.384 --> 01:04:38.220
Wars turned me into
a promiscuous woman, Ingrid.


01:04:38.303 --> 01:04:39.679
Good.


01:04:41.848 --> 01:04:43.392
Are you still in touch with him?


01:04:43.475 --> 01:04:45.102
- With who?
- Damian.


01:04:46.395 --> 01:04:47.396
Um...


01:04:48.105 --> 01:04:49.523
You know, from time to time.


01:04:52.109 --> 01:04:55.070
<i>"How bad can it get?"</i>


01:04:56.530 --> 01:04:57.572
Well


01:04:58.448 --> 01:05:01.618
much worse than you imagine,
Damian, honey.


01:05:05.330 --> 01:05:06.331
Hey.


01:05:07.541 --> 01:05:08.541
Are you all right?


01:05:09.501 --> 01:05:10.627
I was trying to write.


01:05:12.254 --> 01:05:13.255
I can't.


01:05:16.383 --> 01:05:19.928
In this war, I'm incapable
of writing anything.


01:05:20.679 --> 01:05:21.721
What about reading?


01:05:23.014 --> 01:05:24.015
You love to read.


01:05:24.766 --> 01:05:25.934
I've tried.


01:05:27.769 --> 01:05:30.147
I've tried with some of
my favorite writers.


01:05:32.357 --> 01:05:34.818
The spell just isn't there anymore.


01:05:37.571 --> 01:05:39.364
I'm talking about Faulkner,


01:05:40.782 --> 01:05:41.867
Hemingway...


01:05:43.785 --> 01:05:45.203
I can't concentrate.


01:05:46.788 --> 01:05:50.125
My mind just flies off into the void.


01:05:51.418 --> 01:05:52.961
If you're too tired,


01:05:54.463 --> 01:05:55.505
I could read to you.


01:05:58.592 --> 01:05:59.593
Not just reading,


01:06:01.178 --> 01:06:03.138
all pleasure's been reduced.


01:06:05.724 --> 01:06:09.186
It's hard to know
what to pay attention to anymore.


01:06:12.439 --> 01:06:13.773
I have very little time,


01:06:14.900 --> 01:06:16.234
and I don't want to waste it.


01:06:18.403 --> 01:06:19.863
Okay. Um...


01:06:23.283 --> 01:06:26.578
What about music?


01:06:29.164 --> 01:06:31.291
I can only listen to the birds singing.


01:06:32.584 --> 01:06:35.754
Well, luckily, they give us
a serenade every day.


01:06:35.837 --> 01:06:38.298
Music decenters me.


01:06:39.007 --> 01:06:41.843
It comes between me
and whatever it is I'm doing,


01:06:41.927 --> 01:06:43.470
even if it's just thinking.


01:06:44.930 --> 01:06:48.099
Maybe the chemo
is affecting my hearing.


01:06:48.183 --> 01:06:49.351
Oh, honey.


01:06:50.602 --> 01:06:53.522
I've been reduced to very little of myself.


01:07:01.988 --> 01:07:05.075
I long for some peace of body and mind.


01:07:07.869 --> 01:07:10.997
And to just talk whenever
I'm invaded by memory.


01:07:12.249 --> 01:07:13.500
Am I talking too much?


01:07:13.583 --> 01:07:15.627
No, no, no, no. Talk all you want,


01:07:15.710 --> 01:07:17.212
I love listening to you.


01:10:02.252 --> 01:10:03.253
What's going on?


01:10:03.962 --> 01:10:05.547
What's wrong?


01:10:08.174 --> 01:10:09.485
Your door was closed,


01:10:09.509 --> 01:10:10.510
so I thought you...


01:10:12.011 --> 01:10:13.972
Oh, I'm so sorry.


01:10:14.514 --> 01:10:16.266
I opened the window


01:10:16.891 --> 01:10:18.685
and the breeze must have closed it.


01:10:18.768 --> 01:10:19.853
Oh, my God!


01:10:27.152 --> 01:10:28.903
Do you think it's fair to be mad at me


01:10:28.987 --> 01:10:30.655
because I'm still alive?


01:10:33.950 --> 01:10:35.952
Think of it as a rehearsal.


01:10:37.537 --> 01:10:39.289
Now you know how it's gonna be.


01:10:40.582 --> 01:10:42.125
You know how you're gonna feel.


01:10:44.043 --> 01:10:45.879
You're gonna have to make some calls


01:10:46.421 --> 01:10:49.007
and act out all the things
we talked about.


01:10:49.966 --> 01:10:51.801
And you never knew anything,


01:10:52.802 --> 01:10:54.137
and we were on vacation...


01:10:54.220 --> 01:10:55.930
Please, just stop!


01:10:57.724 --> 01:10:58.933
Okay.


01:12:08.628 --> 01:12:10.004
Should we call it a night?


01:12:12.131 --> 01:12:14.759
Or does the young lady
wanna keep watching movies?


01:12:16.594 --> 01:12:19.514
Did you tell me
that they have <i>The Dead?</i>


01:12:20.849 --> 01:12:22.308
Or did I dream that?


01:12:22.392 --> 01:12:23.977
Yeah, they have it.


01:12:24.060 --> 01:12:26.104
Um, do you wanna watch it?


01:12:26.855 --> 01:12:28.314
Yes, please.


01:12:28.398 --> 01:12:29.482
Here we go.


01:12:32.151 --> 01:12:33.194
Here we go.


01:12:43.705 --> 01:12:46.332
<i>Yes, the newspapers are right.</i>


01:12:46.875 --> 01:12:50.712
<i>Snow is general all over Ireland.</i>


01:12:50.795 --> 01:12:54.632
<i>Falling on every part
of the dark central plain,</i>


01:12:54.716 --> 01:12:57.176
<i>on the treeless hills.</i>


01:12:57.802 --> 01:13:00.889
<i>Softly upon the Bog of Allen</i>


01:13:00.972 --> 01:13:04.893
<i>and farther westward, softly falling</i>


01:13:04.976 --> 01:13:09.063
<i>into the dark mutinous Shannon waves.</i>


01:13:10.148 --> 01:13:13.067
<i>One by one, we're all becoming shades.</i>


01:13:15.486 --> 01:13:17.530
<i>Snow is falling,</i>


01:13:18.865 --> 01:13:21.159
<i>falling in that lonely churchyard</i>


01:13:21.242 --> 01:13:23.119
<i>where Michael Furey lies buried.</i>


01:13:24.954 --> 01:13:27.206
<i>Falling faintly through the universe</i>


01:13:27.290 --> 01:13:29.375
<i>and faintly falling,</i>


01:13:30.460 --> 01:13:33.004
<i>like the descent of their last end,</i>


01:13:34.464 --> 01:13:37.926
<i>upon all the living and the dead.</i>


01:13:57.570 --> 01:13:58.570
Do you hear them?


01:13:59.155 --> 01:14:00.198
Mm-hmm.


01:14:08.748 --> 01:14:09.749
It's daytime,


01:14:14.420 --> 01:14:15.672
and you're alive.


01:14:26.265 --> 01:14:27.850
Oh, this is too much.


01:14:27.934 --> 01:14:29.143
- Yeah?
- This is harder


01:14:29.227 --> 01:14:30.687
- than I thought it'd be.
- Okay.


01:14:33.231 --> 01:14:34.440
I think I need to sit.


01:14:34.524 --> 01:14:36.734
All right. Yeah, let's go sit over here.


01:14:37.402 --> 01:14:38.903
Here, let me help you.


01:14:43.074 --> 01:14:45.576
Hey, I've got you. Here we go.


01:14:46.369 --> 01:14:47.412
Here you go.


01:14:48.746 --> 01:14:49.914
Okay.


01:14:53.543 --> 01:14:55.628
- That's much better.
- Oh, good.


01:14:59.716 --> 01:15:02.176
Before coming here, I made a new will.


01:15:02.927 --> 01:15:05.513
Aw, let's not talk about this now, please.


01:15:07.140 --> 01:15:09.308
I'm leaving the apartment
and everything in it


01:15:09.392 --> 01:15:11.019
to Michelle and you.


01:15:16.774 --> 01:15:18.901
I found your war journals in your desk.


01:15:20.069 --> 01:15:21.904
What do you want us to do with them?


01:15:22.572 --> 01:15:23.823
Is it okay if I read them?


01:15:24.449 --> 01:15:25.867
Of course you can read them.


01:15:29.328 --> 01:15:30.955
Can I tell your story?


01:15:31.039 --> 01:15:32.415
You can do what you want.


01:15:33.458 --> 01:15:34.625
I won't be here.


01:15:36.836 --> 01:15:37.879
Can I say that?


01:15:38.504 --> 01:15:39.505
No.


01:15:40.715 --> 01:15:41.716
Okay.


01:16:35.895 --> 01:16:37.647
Let's not talk about this now, okay?


01:16:38.940 --> 01:16:41.442
All right, I'll see you there. Bye.


01:16:48.658 --> 01:16:49.659
<i>Dear Ingrid,</i>


01:16:50.409 --> 01:16:54.705
<i>Today is such a beautiful day
that it seemed to me it...</i>


01:16:56.707 --> 01:16:57.707
Hey.


01:16:58.209 --> 01:16:59.252
Hi.


01:16:59.335 --> 01:17:01.254
- Everything okay?
- Yeah.


01:17:01.337 --> 01:17:03.339
This breeze is delicious.


01:17:03.422 --> 01:17:05.591
Be careful, it's a little chilly.


01:17:07.135 --> 01:17:08.219
Um...


01:17:08.302 --> 01:17:10.513
If you don't need me,
I'm gonna go to the gym.


01:17:10.596 --> 01:17:11.973
But I can stay if you want.


01:17:12.056 --> 01:17:14.350
No. Please, go.
I don't want to be a downer.


01:17:14.433 --> 01:17:15.768
You're not a downer.


01:17:15.852 --> 01:17:17.478
You've been pretty well-behaved.


01:17:18.312 --> 01:17:20.648
Have you talked
to your trainer about me?


01:17:21.858 --> 01:17:23.234
Um...


01:17:23.317 --> 01:17:25.653
Well... I mean, it came up.


01:17:26.237 --> 01:17:28.573
I was talking about being in good shape


01:17:28.656 --> 01:17:31.576
and the heart beating to survive.


01:17:31.659 --> 01:17:34.704
You know, everything that you
talked about in the hospital


01:17:34.787 --> 01:17:36.956
and he looked at me like I was a lunatic,


01:17:37.039 --> 01:17:40.334
so I told him I had a friend
who was sick. That's all.


01:17:41.836 --> 01:17:46.632
Just remember,
you know nothing about anything.


01:17:46.716 --> 01:17:47.758
Mm.


01:17:52.096 --> 01:17:53.806
Come here, give me a kiss.


01:17:56.475 --> 01:17:57.475
- You okay?
- Yes.


01:18:20.750 --> 01:18:22.001
- Hi.
- Hi.


01:18:27.215 --> 01:18:29.592
I lied to her, I don't like it.


01:18:29.675 --> 01:18:30.968
Well, you'll have to practice.


01:18:31.052 --> 01:18:32.053
Lying?


01:18:32.136 --> 01:18:35.848
Yes. Officially, you aren't aware
of Martha's intentions.


01:18:36.390 --> 01:18:37.391
Yeah.


01:18:37.475 --> 01:18:39.936
And I found a lawyer,
in case you need one.


01:18:40.019 --> 01:18:42.063
Thank you. Let's not talk about this now.


01:18:42.146 --> 01:18:44.190
- Mm.
- How'd your lecture go?


01:18:45.691 --> 01:18:48.778
Well, they weren't too happy
about my not taking questions.


01:18:50.196 --> 01:18:51.239
In the end,


01:18:52.740 --> 01:18:55.785
people started muttering
and someone called me a coward.


01:18:55.868 --> 01:18:57.578
It doesn't bother me.


01:18:57.662 --> 01:18:59.705
I spent way too much time


01:18:59.789 --> 01:19:01.958
caring about my reputation,
and for what?


01:19:02.625 --> 01:19:04.853
So, what are you doing
with all that time you've gotten back?


01:19:04.877 --> 01:19:07.421
Are you doing more of what you love?


01:19:08.756 --> 01:19:11.217
I have to admit that my interest in things


01:19:11.300 --> 01:19:13.678
has been shrinking as I get older.


01:19:15.346 --> 01:19:17.556
Martha said the same thing
a couple days ago.


01:19:17.640 --> 01:19:20.142
There are so few things left
that she can really enjoy.


01:19:20.226 --> 01:19:22.019
- I understand.
- Mm.


01:19:23.229 --> 01:19:24.563
But you're not sick.


01:19:24.647 --> 01:19:27.024
No, but I feel the same way,
especially after the pandemic.


01:19:27.108 --> 01:19:29.402
I don't go to the cinema
or listen to music.


01:19:30.236 --> 01:19:31.279
I... I read a lot,


01:19:32.029 --> 01:19:33.948
but only subjects to do with my lectures.


01:19:34.031 --> 01:19:36.450
Mm. You still go to galleries?
You used to love that.


01:19:36.534 --> 01:19:38.095
When we were together,
we'd go all the time


01:19:38.119 --> 01:19:40.246
and talk about how powerful the art is.


01:19:40.329 --> 01:19:41.372
You still like that?


01:19:42.540 --> 01:19:45.209
Even if every poet in the world
sat down to write a poem


01:19:45.293 --> 01:19:47.712
about the climate crisis,
it wouldn't save one tree.


01:19:47.795 --> 01:19:49.880
At least you're still
interested in the trees.


01:19:49.964 --> 01:19:51.590
I'm interested in sex, too.


01:19:51.674 --> 01:19:53.342
Well, then you're not that bad.


01:19:53.426 --> 01:19:55.845
When I was young,


01:19:55.928 --> 01:19:59.849
if a day went by without sex,
I thought it was incomplete.


01:19:59.932 --> 01:20:00.975
I remember that.


01:20:01.058 --> 01:20:06.188
I'm not nostalgic,
but I miss the nights when we'd drink,


01:20:07.273 --> 01:20:09.859
and take drugs, have sex,


01:20:09.942 --> 01:20:12.903
all that didn't distract us
from what we really wanted to do.


01:20:12.987 --> 01:20:15.406
You drank and you took drugs.


01:20:15.489 --> 01:20:17.325
I mean, more than I did anyway.


01:20:17.408 --> 01:20:18.593
I don't know how much you drank,


01:20:18.617 --> 01:20:22.079
but you always acted as you were
as blitzed as the rest of us.


01:20:22.997 --> 01:20:25.291
But you were an essential part
of the party.


01:20:26.125 --> 01:20:29.628
That is, until you got bored
and went off to discover Europe.


01:20:31.088 --> 01:20:32.340
You want to talk about that?


01:20:33.632 --> 01:20:34.712
Tell me about your lecture.


01:20:36.218 --> 01:20:39.597
I admit that I've become
something of a monomaniac.


01:20:40.598 --> 01:20:42.516
My own son is no longer speaking to me


01:20:42.600 --> 01:20:44.894
because I didn't hide how appalled I was


01:20:44.977 --> 01:20:47.563
that his wife is expecting another child.


01:20:47.646 --> 01:20:48.874
He doesn't want me anywhere near her


01:20:48.898 --> 01:20:50.292
for fear she'll have a miscarriage.


01:20:50.316 --> 01:20:53.069
What? How could you tell him
that he can't have another child?


01:20:53.152 --> 01:20:55.488
- It's their third!
- What...


01:20:55.571 --> 01:20:57.656
So, what's the next logical alternative?


01:20:57.740 --> 01:20:59.176
For people to start killing themselves?


01:20:59.200 --> 01:21:01.410
People should be aware,
once and for all,


01:21:01.494 --> 01:21:03.662
of the state of the fucking
planet they're living on.


01:21:05.623 --> 01:21:08.667
Well, perhaps this isn't
the best subject for you.


01:21:08.751 --> 01:21:12.421
You're living with
a dying woman in a world


01:21:12.505 --> 01:21:14.715
also in its death throes.


01:21:17.176 --> 01:21:19.804
Do you really think the situation
is that desperate?


01:21:19.887 --> 01:21:23.265
Yes. Read the science
and see what the world is doing with it.


01:21:24.433 --> 01:21:28.437
They're releasing more CO2
into the air than ever before.


01:21:28.521 --> 01:21:32.024
Sooner or later,
and I fear it will be sooner,


01:21:32.108 --> 01:21:35.277
all this will be shot to hell, yeah.


01:21:35.361 --> 01:21:38.906
Nothing is going to hasten
the end of the planet


01:21:38.989 --> 01:21:41.951
more than the survival of neo-liberalism


01:21:42.034 --> 01:21:43.619
and the rise of the far right.


01:21:43.702 --> 01:21:47.581
And we have both of them here,
marching side by side.


01:21:50.918 --> 01:21:54.046
Sorry, I didn't want to bring you down,


01:21:55.339 --> 01:21:57.383
but I get riled up with this.


01:21:57.466 --> 01:22:00.428
You cannot go around telling people
that there's no hope.


01:22:00.970 --> 01:22:01.970
It's tragic.


01:22:02.638 --> 01:22:05.266
And maybe it's really
unpleasant of me to say so,


01:22:05.349 --> 01:22:09.228
but I've completely lost faith
in people doing the right thing.


01:22:09.311 --> 01:22:12.356
I'm living every day expecting to find
Martha's body in her bed,


01:22:12.440 --> 01:22:16.360
but that doesn't stop me
from enjoying every minute with her,


01:22:16.444 --> 01:22:17.695
just the opposite.


01:22:18.529 --> 01:22:20.990
I'm learning from her
and you should, too,


01:22:21.949 --> 01:22:24.869
because there are lots of ways
to live inside a tragedy.


01:22:26.745 --> 01:22:28.706
Of course it's painful,


01:22:29.415 --> 01:22:31.459
but I can take it.


01:22:32.543 --> 01:22:34.753
And I'm trying to live


01:22:34.837 --> 01:22:36.797
with the same joy that she has,


01:22:37.548 --> 01:22:39.508
and with the same appreciation, so


01:22:40.426 --> 01:22:42.428
the last thing I need
is a speech like yours.


01:22:43.345 --> 01:22:44.805
I've always admired you for that.


01:22:46.182 --> 01:22:47.057
What?


01:22:47.141 --> 01:22:50.186
You're one of the only people
who knows how to suffer


01:22:50.269 --> 01:22:52.855
without making others feel guilty about it.


01:23:35.481 --> 01:23:37.441
Do you think it will be much longer?


01:23:37.525 --> 01:23:40.778
No, it'll be soon. Any day now.


01:23:42.071 --> 01:23:43.948
You have to be prepared.


01:23:44.031 --> 01:23:45.366
I know the police.


01:23:45.449 --> 01:23:47.243
They'll ask you all sorts of questions,


01:23:47.326 --> 01:23:49.662
they'll dig into your relationship
like scavengers.


01:23:50.246 --> 01:23:51.997
You need a kind of mental script.


01:23:52.081 --> 01:23:54.041
No, I thought about it, I do have it.


01:23:54.959 --> 01:23:57.878
Good. Stay strong and stick to your story.


01:23:57.962 --> 01:23:59.505
And when it happens,


01:23:59.588 --> 01:24:02.091
you should call the police
before you call me.


01:24:02.174 --> 01:24:03.443
No, I need to call her daughter.


01:24:03.467 --> 01:24:05.010
I should call her before I call you.


01:24:05.094 --> 01:24:07.513
Okay, but be careful what you say to her.


01:24:07.596 --> 01:24:10.224
I had to tell the lawyer
about the situation.


01:24:10.307 --> 01:24:12.893
Why do we have to go through all this,
like we're criminals?


01:24:13.727 --> 01:24:16.772
Shouldn't dying people have the right
to end their lives with dignity?


01:24:16.855 --> 01:24:19.191
They will, once
our teetering health system


01:24:19.275 --> 01:24:20.734
completely collapses.


01:24:57.896 --> 01:24:58.897
Martha?


01:25:19.627 --> 01:25:20.628
<i>Dear Ingrid,</i>


01:25:21.378 --> 01:25:23.714
<i>today is such a beautiful day</i>


01:25:24.298 --> 01:25:27.051
<i>that it seemed to me
it was the moment to leave.</i>


01:25:27.760 --> 01:25:30.888
<i>It consoled me that you weren't
in the room downstairs,</i>


01:25:31.513 --> 01:25:33.766
<i>even though that was the idea.</i>


01:25:33.849 --> 01:25:36.560
<i>But you know I always improvise</i>


01:25:37.478 --> 01:25:39.271
<i>and I'm almost happy that,</i>


01:25:39.355 --> 01:25:41.649
<i>while I fade away on the lounger,</i>


01:25:42.524 --> 01:25:44.318
<i>you're out in the world,</i>


01:25:44.401 --> 01:25:47.071
<i>experiencing something
different to my death.</i>


01:25:48.489 --> 01:25:51.700
<i>No one will be able
to accuse you of complicity.</i>


01:25:52.993 --> 01:25:54.578
<i>You have accompanied me</i>


01:25:54.662 --> 01:25:57.998
<i>as much as any human being
can accompany another.</i>


01:25:59.458 --> 01:26:02.419
<i>Call my daughter and tell her I'm sorry.</i>


01:26:03.712 --> 01:26:06.173
<i>And thank you, love.</i>


01:26:31.782 --> 01:26:32.825
Martha.


01:26:36.495 --> 01:26:38.080
I'll do whatever you want.


01:27:05.649 --> 01:27:08.318
We had dinner and then we watched
a Buster Keaton movie.


01:27:08.402 --> 01:27:09.820
I told you this already.


01:27:09.903 --> 01:27:11.989
And you didn't notice anything strange,


01:27:12.072 --> 01:27:14.199
anything that made you suspect...


01:27:16.785 --> 01:27:17.828
Try to remember.


01:27:17.911 --> 01:27:20.831
I remember it perfectly,
it was a fun night.


01:27:20.914 --> 01:27:23.584
There were no gestures?
Nothing she said?


01:27:23.667 --> 01:27:26.503
We said goodnight
and then I went upstairs


01:27:26.587 --> 01:27:29.089
and I stayed up late reading a book


01:27:29.173 --> 01:27:31.800
that Martha had recommended
called <i>Erotic Vagrancy.</i>


01:27:31.884 --> 01:27:34.636
It's about Elizabeth Taylor
and Richard Burton.


01:27:34.720 --> 01:27:36.180
- Do you know it?
- No.


01:27:36.263 --> 01:27:38.849
Martha and I both thought
that it was really fun.


01:27:38.932 --> 01:27:41.185
Try to answer
only the questions I ask you.


01:27:45.230 --> 01:27:46.670
What'd you do the following morning?


01:27:49.026 --> 01:27:50.235
I had lunch with a friend.


01:27:51.236 --> 01:27:53.363
And when I came back,
I called out for her


01:27:53.447 --> 01:27:55.157
and when she didn't answer,


01:27:55.240 --> 01:27:56.325
I went to her bedroom.


01:27:57.117 --> 01:27:58.160
But she wasn't there.


01:27:59.161 --> 01:28:00.454
So I went into the backyard


01:28:01.079 --> 01:28:03.248
and that's when I saw her.


01:28:03.332 --> 01:28:06.168
And, at first, I thought that
she was asleep on the lounge chair


01:28:06.251 --> 01:28:09.087
and I got really nervous
and I called the ambulance.


01:28:09.171 --> 01:28:10.589
And they got there very quickly


01:28:10.672 --> 01:28:12.341
and then the EMTs saw her


01:28:12.424 --> 01:28:14.760
and then they said there was nothing
that they could do.


01:28:15.427 --> 01:28:16.845
Nobody buys this pill by accident


01:28:16.929 --> 01:28:19.598
if they're not thinking of suicide
or killing someone,


01:28:19.681 --> 01:28:21.308
so, you didn't know anything about this?


01:28:21.391 --> 01:28:22.267
About what?


01:28:22.351 --> 01:28:24.937
About her being in possession
of this illegal compound.


01:28:25.020 --> 01:28:28.524
No. She was taking medication
for the pain,


01:28:28.607 --> 01:28:30.484
you know, patches and pills, but she


01:28:30.567 --> 01:28:32.694
she never shared the specifics with me.


01:28:33.779 --> 01:28:35.531
It is strange that,


01:28:35.614 --> 01:28:37.032
if you two were such good friends,


01:28:37.115 --> 01:28:39.284
that she didn't say anything to you.


01:28:40.369 --> 01:28:44.873
You can't just walk into a drugstore
and buy this pill.


01:28:45.999 --> 01:28:47.459
It's very difficult to come by.


01:28:48.877 --> 01:28:51.338
I think when she rented the house,


01:28:52.089 --> 01:28:54.716
she already knew what she was
gonna do, right?


01:28:54.800 --> 01:28:56.051
It's possible,


01:28:56.718 --> 01:28:58.303
but she didn't tell me anything.


01:28:59.263 --> 01:29:01.139
She was exhausted
from the last treatment


01:29:01.223 --> 01:29:02.909
and she wanted to take a break
before going back


01:29:02.933 --> 01:29:04.309
for the next round of chemo.


01:29:05.060 --> 01:29:06.854
She wasn't the type to throw in the towel.


01:29:06.937 --> 01:29:08.063
She didn't complain?


01:29:09.022 --> 01:29:11.483
She didn't say anything
that made you sense


01:29:13.026 --> 01:29:14.027
the end?


01:29:14.778 --> 01:29:16.298
It was a great responsibility for you.


01:29:17.447 --> 01:29:19.032
She complained sometimes.


01:29:21.535 --> 01:29:24.329
What did she complain about?
What did she say?


01:29:26.123 --> 01:29:28.166
She'd lost the capacity for attention.


01:29:29.501 --> 01:29:33.255
She couldn't read or write, for example.


01:29:35.424 --> 01:29:37.050
Her life was reduced to surviving.


01:29:37.134 --> 01:29:40.470
You know, I find it very hard to believe


01:29:40.554 --> 01:29:42.931
that she didn't say anything
that made you suspect the end.


01:29:43.015 --> 01:29:45.350
It was more than evident
that she was very sick,


01:29:45.434 --> 01:29:48.114
but she wanted to take a vacation
before going back to the hospital.


01:29:48.145 --> 01:29:49.688
I told you this already.


01:29:50.689 --> 01:29:55.861
So, we also spoke to some of
Martha's close friends.


01:29:57.821 --> 01:30:00.908
In general, they all coincide
with your testimony.


01:30:03.035 --> 01:30:05.746
But one of them, Stella Byrne,


01:30:05.829 --> 01:30:08.332
told us that, after Martha
finished her chemotherapy,


01:30:08.415 --> 01:30:11.293
that she proposed
that she accompany her


01:30:11.376 --> 01:30:13.754
to a house in the country


01:30:13.837 --> 01:30:16.757
where she intended to commit suicide.


01:30:20.719 --> 01:30:22.930
Asked her to, and I quote...


01:30:24.389 --> 01:30:25.557
"Be in the room next door."


01:30:29.102 --> 01:30:30.646
And her friend refused.


01:30:31.521 --> 01:30:34.691
I wasn't in the room next door,
I was in the room downstairs.


01:30:34.775 --> 01:30:35.984
When I spoke to Mrs. Byrne


01:30:36.068 --> 01:30:37.128
and informed her of the suicide,


01:30:37.152 --> 01:30:38.528
she told me she wasn't surprised.


01:30:39.488 --> 01:30:42.240
There's another word for Martha did,
it's called euthanasia.


01:30:42.324 --> 01:30:43.867
Well, call it what you want,


01:30:43.951 --> 01:30:47.579
but, for me, what your friend
did is a crime


01:30:47.663 --> 01:30:50.749
and, as a policeman, as a human being,


01:30:50.832 --> 01:30:51.875
as a man of faith,


01:30:53.335 --> 01:30:55.921
I'm radically opposed
to anyone committing a crime.


01:30:57.297 --> 01:30:59.341
And, of course, anyone aiding
and abetting in one.


01:31:12.312 --> 01:31:14.606
Damian, can you come down
to the police station, please?


01:31:15.315 --> 01:31:16.316
This is endless.


01:31:16.400 --> 01:31:19.903
How do you explain
that your friend Martha


01:31:19.987 --> 01:31:21.571
was so explicit with Mrs. Byrne


01:31:21.655 --> 01:31:23.936
and yet she didn't tell you
anything about her intentions?


01:31:23.991 --> 01:31:25.701
I'm not gonna say another word.


01:31:25.784 --> 01:31:28.078
If I'm under arrest,
then tell me the charges.


01:31:28.161 --> 01:31:30.122
Otherwise, I'll wait
in the hall for my lawyer.


01:31:30.205 --> 01:31:31.456
Very foresighted of you.


01:31:31.540 --> 01:31:33.059
What made you think
you'd need a lawyer?


01:31:33.083 --> 01:31:35.961
Why don't you ask your friend,
he witnessed the interrogation.


01:31:36.920 --> 01:31:39.506
I think you're lying.


01:31:41.133 --> 01:31:43.253
And that you're the kind of person
who wouldn't say no


01:31:43.301 --> 01:31:45.804
if a friend asked you
for help committing suicide.


01:31:48.348 --> 01:31:49.474
Let her go.


01:31:58.525 --> 01:31:59.526
Hey.


01:32:00.110 --> 01:32:01.570
- Hi.
- Hi.


01:32:01.653 --> 01:32:03.655
- How are you?
- I'm okay.


01:32:04.197 --> 01:32:06.033
This is my lawyer, Sarah.


01:32:06.116 --> 01:32:07.868
- Hi. Pleasure.
- Thank you for coming.


01:32:07.951 --> 01:32:09.453
Of course. Damian's filled me in.


01:32:09.536 --> 01:32:11.736
Is there anything I should know
about the interrogation?


01:32:11.788 --> 01:32:13.623
Well, he treated me like I was the killer.


01:32:13.707 --> 01:32:15.459
- But you were with me.
- He doesn't care.


01:32:15.542 --> 01:32:16.918
He insists that I'm implicated.


01:32:17.002 --> 01:32:18.045
Okay, but...


01:32:18.128 --> 01:32:20.547
He spoke to a friend
of Martha, Stella Byrne,


01:32:20.630 --> 01:32:22.591
who said that Martha
had approached her first


01:32:22.674 --> 01:32:24.051
and she refused to help her.


01:32:24.134 --> 01:32:26.053
Okay, well, I'm sure
everything was recorded.


01:32:26.136 --> 01:32:27.471
Mm-hmm.


01:32:27.554 --> 01:32:30.640
Um, and this police officer
witnessed everything.


01:32:30.724 --> 01:32:31.933
You can come in now.


01:32:32.017 --> 01:32:33.643
I'll go in alone. I'm her attorney.


01:32:35.604 --> 01:32:37.272
Don't worry, this is all very clear.


01:32:39.608 --> 01:32:40.776
Thank you for coming.


01:32:40.859 --> 01:32:42.027
My pleasure.


01:32:42.652 --> 01:32:44.863
Jesus! What an asshole!


01:32:44.946 --> 01:32:46.586
I've never been treated like that before.


01:32:47.616 --> 01:32:50.096
You were unlucky enough
to come up against a religious fanatic,


01:32:50.160 --> 01:32:51.554
but he's not gonna bother you again.


01:32:51.578 --> 01:32:52.788
I'm gonna file a complaint.


01:32:52.871 --> 01:32:54.998
Thank you so much for everything.


01:32:55.082 --> 01:32:57.125
You still need to be available
for the next 48 hours


01:32:57.209 --> 01:32:59.044
until forensic formalities are done.


01:33:00.045 --> 01:33:02.089
Um, I told them to call me if necessary.


01:33:02.172 --> 01:33:03.173
I'll be at the house.


01:33:03.256 --> 01:33:04.650
Do you have
all the information you need?


01:33:04.674 --> 01:33:05.926
Yes, Damian gave it to me.


01:33:06.718 --> 01:33:08.845
Just give me a call
if anything comes up, okay?


01:33:08.929 --> 01:33:10.514
I'm gonna head back to the office.


01:33:10.597 --> 01:33:11.837
I'm really sorry for your loss.


01:33:11.890 --> 01:33:13.183
- Thank you.
- Thanks, Sarah.


01:33:13.266 --> 01:33:14.267
Bye.


01:33:15.185 --> 01:33:16.978
I can't believe Stella told him that.


01:33:17.062 --> 01:33:18.289
Well, he probably cornered her,


01:33:18.313 --> 01:33:20.607
and they have Martha's computer
and her cell phone.


01:33:20.690 --> 01:33:21.733
Mm.


01:33:21.817 --> 01:33:22.877
Do you know if they talked?


01:33:22.901 --> 01:33:25.737
No, I don't know,
she didn't tell me anything.


01:33:26.905 --> 01:33:28.281
What do you wanna do?


01:33:28.365 --> 01:33:30.909
I need to go back to the house
and pack up Martha's things.


01:33:30.992 --> 01:33:32.911
Sorry.


01:33:34.454 --> 01:33:35.455
Hello?


01:33:36.081 --> 01:33:37.332
Uh, speaking.


01:33:39.417 --> 01:33:40.752
It's Michelle.


01:33:40.836 --> 01:33:42.003
Martha's daughter?


01:33:42.838 --> 01:33:44.047
Yes, of course.


01:33:44.131 --> 01:33:46.216
No, no, of course you can come over.


01:33:46.299 --> 01:33:49.553
I'm headed there right now.
I'll text you the address.


01:33:50.929 --> 01:33:53.014
Okay, I'll see you soon. Bye.


01:33:55.016 --> 01:33:57.727
Wow. Wow.


01:33:57.811 --> 01:33:59.771
I'm headed back to the city,


01:33:59.855 --> 01:34:02.691
so tell me when you're back
and I'll help you with your move.


01:34:03.859 --> 01:34:05.777
Thank you for everything.


01:34:08.613 --> 01:34:10.866
And you can tell me
how it went with Michelle.


01:34:11.491 --> 01:34:12.491
I will.


01:34:14.369 --> 01:34:16.580
- Thanks. I'll call you, okay?
- Okay. Take care.


01:34:50.280 --> 01:34:51.531
Hello, I'm Michelle.


01:34:52.407 --> 01:34:53.408
I'm Ingrid.


01:34:54.534 --> 01:34:55.534
Hi.


01:34:58.955 --> 01:35:00.707
Let's go inside, okay?


01:35:00.790 --> 01:35:01.790
Yeah.


01:35:04.836 --> 01:35:05.837
Come on in.


01:35:12.052 --> 01:35:13.762
Do you wanna see your mother's room?


01:35:13.845 --> 01:35:15.013
Yes, please.


01:35:15.597 --> 01:35:17.474
It's right down there. Right down the hall.


01:35:45.585 --> 01:35:47.045
I made some coffee.


01:35:47.128 --> 01:35:48.421
Would you like some?


01:35:48.505 --> 01:35:50.173
Uh, I also have tea.


01:35:50.257 --> 01:35:51.925
No, coffee's great. Thank you.


01:35:52.717 --> 01:35:53.718
Here you go.


01:35:58.306 --> 01:35:59.599
Did she tell you about me?


01:35:59.683 --> 01:36:01.059
Of course she did.


01:36:03.019 --> 01:36:06.398
And she told me you were very upset
that you never met your father.


01:36:07.357 --> 01:36:08.817
So she told you about my father?


01:36:08.900 --> 01:36:10.277
She did.


01:36:11.361 --> 01:36:13.405
Don't you think
she could have helped him


01:36:13.488 --> 01:36:14.823
when he came back from the war?


01:36:15.407 --> 01:36:17.909
She helped him as best she could.


01:36:17.993 --> 01:36:21.079
Your father came back
very badly damaged


01:36:21.162 --> 01:36:23.832
and he wanted to move to another city
and start a new life.


01:36:23.915 --> 01:36:27.085
His plans never included you or Martha.


01:36:27.794 --> 01:36:31.506
And your mother accepted
the end of the relationship and...


01:36:32.882 --> 01:36:34.592
And she saw him in such a bad way


01:36:34.676 --> 01:36:36.803
that she gave him a kiss
to give him some peace


01:36:36.886 --> 01:36:39.097
and that kiss turned
into something more.


01:36:41.182 --> 01:36:43.059
And you are the fruit of that moment.


01:36:44.644 --> 01:36:47.439
My mother never told me
anything about that.


01:36:47.522 --> 01:36:49.691
It's a difficult thing
to explain to a child.


01:36:49.774 --> 01:36:51.401
She could have told me later.


01:36:52.444 --> 01:36:53.778
By then you were so estranged


01:36:53.862 --> 01:36:55.739
that she didn't feel
it was possible anymore.


01:36:57.198 --> 01:36:59.367
She was a teenager,


01:36:59.451 --> 01:37:00.702
she had a life to live,


01:37:00.785 --> 01:37:04.873
and your father moved to San Diego
and he made no effort to know you.


01:37:15.967 --> 01:37:17.218
So, Ingrid,


01:37:19.179 --> 01:37:22.390
do you think I was totally mistaken
about Martha?


01:37:23.475 --> 01:37:24.726
You were unfair,


01:37:26.394 --> 01:37:29.606
but no one can blame you
for wanting to know who your father was.


01:37:32.650 --> 01:37:34.027
It's a sad story,


01:37:34.110 --> 01:37:35.987
it was very painful for both of you.


01:37:39.824 --> 01:37:41.701
Don't be so hard on yourself,


01:37:41.785 --> 01:37:43.328
Martha wasn't the perfect mother.


01:37:44.996 --> 01:37:46.289
No, she wasn't.


01:37:50.919 --> 01:37:52.587
Can I stay here tonight?


01:37:52.670 --> 01:37:55.507
Yes, of course.
This is your mother's house!


01:37:59.344 --> 01:38:00.387
<i>Dear Martha,</i>


01:38:01.596 --> 01:38:04.474
<i>I thought you'd like to know
I've come back to the house in the woods</i>


01:38:04.557 --> 01:38:06.059
<i>to gather up your things.</i>


01:38:08.353 --> 01:38:10.063
<i>Your daughter came to see me.</i>


01:38:10.939 --> 01:38:12.482
<i>I'm still shaking.</i>


01:38:13.525 --> 01:38:15.235
<i>She looks so like you.</i>


01:38:16.403 --> 01:38:19.155
<i>She asked me if she could stay
and sleep in your bed,</i>


01:38:19.864 --> 01:38:21.449
<i>and, of course, I said yes.</i>


01:38:23.576 --> 01:38:25.870
<i>I think your death
has brought her closer to you.</i>


01:38:29.874 --> 01:38:31.918
<i>I never thought I'd inherit her,</i>


01:38:32.752 --> 01:38:34.754
<i>even if it's just for a day.</i>


01:38:35.922 --> 01:38:38.174
<i>The house is filled with you.</i>


01:38:41.136 --> 01:38:43.721
<i>When I came in,
after talking to the police,</i>


01:38:44.931 --> 01:38:47.308
<i>the first thing I saw
was the door of your room,</i>


01:38:48.852 --> 01:38:50.311
<i>and it was open.</i>


01:38:51.521 --> 01:38:54.691
<i>And I said to myself, "She's alive."</i>


01:39:28.558 --> 01:39:30.602
I came out here to listen to the birds.


01:39:33.313 --> 01:39:35.106
Your mother would get up like this,


01:39:36.316 --> 01:39:37.609
at dawn,


01:39:38.818 --> 01:39:39.818
and lie right there.


01:39:45.492 --> 01:39:48.203
Look, it's snowing.


01:39:57.253 --> 01:39:58.588
The snow is falling.


01:40:01.257 --> 01:40:02.634
It's falling on the lonely pool


01:40:02.717 --> 01:40:04.010
we never used.


01:40:06.221 --> 01:40:07.639
It's falling on the woods,


01:40:08.723 --> 01:40:10.892
where we walked and you lay,


01:40:10.975 --> 01:40:13.353
exhausted, on the ground.


01:40:16.064 --> 01:40:18.274
Falling on your daughter and on me.


01:40:21.653 --> 01:40:23.363
Falling upon the living and the dead.

